followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95","id":70842045,"login":"Vadymk95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQyMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-spa-pwa/commits/f2534c11ec6e7c524b9032c2812784e4053eee7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T20:08:28Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T20:08:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): a fork that renames its default branch no longer loses CI and protection (#52)\n\nThe ruleset targets ~DEFAULT_BRANCH, which follows a rename. The workflow triggers\ndid not: they named `master` literally. So a fork whose owner renamed the default\nbranch to `main` got a ruleset demanding a check that no workflow would ever run,\nand every pull request in that repository blocked forever with no error anywhere.\nThe trigger filters now name both branches in all four templates.\n\n`.github/ruleset.json` is new: settings do not travel with a fork, so the only way\nto hand protection over is as a file the forker can post back. It carries the check\nnames these workflows actually produce, so renaming a CI job means editing this file\nin the same commit. README now points at it with the exact command instead of naming\none check in prose, which is also how that sentence stops being wrong here, where the\ncheck is not called `validate`.\n\nRelease: the header comment claimed no CI runs on a release pull request. Measured\ntoday, the runs are created and sit in `action_required`, reporting nothing, which\nis why a release PR shows zero checks and \"Merging is blocked\". The comment now says\nthat, names the one-click approval and the PAT, and says not to reach for an admin\nbypass, which is not selective and would drop the status checks, the pull-request\nrule and the force-push rule together.\n\n`.npmrc` is now byte-identical across the four templates, on the audit floor of\n`high` that this repo already documented: the blocking gate fails on high and\ncritical, so a bare `npm audit` set to `moderate` reports a severity the gate will\nnot block.","tree":{"sha":"2151b183650fb4feccf26468ec1769a53e7c859e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-spa-pwa/git/trees/2151b183650fb4feccf26468ec1769a53e7c859e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-spa-pwa/git/commits/f2534c11ec6e7c524b9032c2812784e4053eee7c","verification":{"payload":"tree 2151b183650fb4feccf26468ec1769a53e7c859e\nparent 637576a61b24357c187bd6b362ba42968fb253de\nauthor Vadym Kononenko <70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com> 1789330108 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789330108 +0300\n\nfix(ci): a fork that renames its default branch no longer loses CI and protection (#52)\n\nThe ruleset targets ~DEFAULT_BRANCH, which follows a rename. The workflow triggers\ndid not: they named `master` literally. So a fork whose owner renamed the default\nbranch to `main` got a ruleset demanding a check that no workflow would ever run,\nand every pull request in that repository blocked forever with no error anywhere.\nThe trigger filters now name both branches in all four templates.\n\n`.github/ruleset.json` is new: settings do not travel with a fork, so the only way\nto hand protection over is as a file the forker can post back. It carries the check\nnames these workflows actually produce, so renaming a CI job means editing this file\nin the same commit. README now points at it with the exact command instead of naming\none check in prose, which is also how that sentence stops being wrong here, where the\ncheck is not called `validate`.\n\nRelease: the header comment claimed no CI runs on a release pull request. Measured\ntoday, the runs are created and sit in `action_required`, reporting nothing, which\nis why a release PR shows zero checks and \"Merging is blocked\". The comment now says\nthat, names the one-click approval and the PAT, and says not to reach for an admin\nbypass, which is not selective and would drop the status checks, the pull-request\nrule and the force-push rule together.\n\n`.npmrc` is now byte-identical across the four templates, on the audit floor of\n`high` that this repo already documented: the blocking gate fails on high and\ncritical, so a bare `npm audit` set to `moderate` reports a severity the gate will\nnot block.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpwK8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMykQAKTBUb3qz2GbiZwduHVXiNmb\n39Pc2Is1p+Vbvwzi4QaYnbqlvhTZkDhHuslQbQaqr+SCj3sWhkYq7OI1Udzg9brC\n91f7VfIYKujQZCt2yDkjoFy7qk4PkWIEmZKHXxFro72TFd9k4RiLOaY7MuQz7Nqo\n5HySd/nGdQVWnctuHYVd4BYQJK65ZDOigavxp0kmHCR+hIAwnyIjnls4LF60hvDR\n7qpA+LnSF0lZCswu5Tn5ixh2wmwzdxJq0mUjpwaewdr/F/p4TVDC+ohiqQJ2a6Iv\nwglnyyaMgkJvUr4F2Z/3TgKCWMroyLvy1zG9JuX2UnoxVEvEyECgJc3LedSnQdPm\nacpMLO29sBhEMeh9oHVhGlTOQCkCg3Im9HjNjwmgujpvUvtHGVb4egqqF0Dpaq2x\nOBUWztGtBwLamTXTNnyEDxTRdyW9n0yweZIpG/DJUEgE6blOvKhoQYH2EpzvB5AN\nn6kjO52M4wSxKGYcAZi/TUjpTYeG/S8/kk0t7uYMWQLbpAzIAa93O1m7eSGVg80h\n1O6X9/j0k/xnWte8+yRvJ2iYOq6t8ItwKPO8mhunvo306x6pAgZ2jo7m1KUWSbcI\nEr49qFOEEBinwT3XT3QqLE9+Y5Uk5LVJX8fT2jEgLDvDhrbMT8kNTllcdsFh9Z3i\nRFha/UMK0pHU2dxuiNPp\n=Zssj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T20:08:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198