r_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-spa-pwa/commits/6158d75e4efbf679437912eda3ce06b7358b21fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:18:37Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:18:37Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"message":"fix(deps): close the extract-zip advisories with a @puppeteer/browsers floor\n\nextract-zip has no fixed release in any major, so the remedy is removing it from the\ntree, not raising it. @puppeteer/browsers 3.0.2 dropped the dependency; a capped floor\n(>=3.0.2 <4) resolves all three copies to 3.2.2 and both chains lose extract-zip:\n\n- @lhci/cli 0.15.1 -> lighthouse 12.6.1 -> puppeteer-core -> @puppeteer/browsers\n- @size-limit/preset-app -> @size-limit/time -> estimo -> find-chrome-bin ->\n  @puppeteer/browsers\n\nnpm''s fixAvailable, a @lhci/cli 0.12.0 downgrade, is rejected per the capped-floor\ndoctrine. puppeteer-core is deliberately NOT overridden: 25.x drops the CJS build that\nestimo imports (puppeteer-core/lib/cjs/puppeteer/revisions.js) and size:check dies on\nit. It stays in 24.x, where lighthouse re-resolved 24.22.0 -> 24.43.1 inside its own\nrange; all 12 symbols puppeteer-core imports from @puppeteer/browsers exist in 3.2.2.\n\nGHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv goes stale the moment extract-zip leaves the tree, and the gate\nfails a stale allowance by design, so the allowance is removed in this same commit.\n\nProofs: audit 10 high -> 0 high / 0 critical; audit:gate red on the stale entry, green\nwithout it; build + size:check green with headless Chrome launched through the estimo\nchain (index entry 25.15 kB of 26 kB); lhci --version 0.15.1 and lhci healthcheck pass.","tree":{"sha":"c6a57d09711f52a184bb4b4b10754449bbeb5808","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-spa-pwa/git/trees/c6a57d09711f52a184bb4b4b10754449bbeb5808"},