b.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/a6586e31d6992aa1fcf38736a8c2ad465b972e6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T17:20:34Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T17:20:34Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"message":"feat(local-dev): one-command native dev stack (dev-up.sh / dev-down.sh)\n\nAddresses the platform review''s top contributor-friction item: cold-starting the\nplatform meant hand-launching six services in order with no launcher. dev-up.sh\nbrings them up natively (no Docker) in dependency order — catalog (Java+H2, no\nexternal DB), ingest, matter-management MFE, agent, Studio, Hub — each\nidempotent (a listening port is left alone) and behind a bounded health gate,\nlogging to platform/local-dev/.logs/. It bakes in SEED_REMOTES for the\nmatter-management remote so the Hub''s matter-* widgets resolve on load (the\n''Unknown widget'' issue won''t recur). dev-down.sh stops by port; both take an\noptional service-name filter. README documents ports, prereqs, and that\nStudio''s local authMode is left untouched.\n\nVerified: run against a partially-down stack, it cold-started the missing\nservices to all-healthy (6/6 200); detached processes survive the launcher exit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"db35780b688ab6b9e6db4a762364b09ab0f8f005","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/db35780b688ab6b9e6db4a762364b09ab0f8f005"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/a6586e31d6992aa1fcf38736a8c2ad465b972e6e","verification":{"payload":"tree db35780b688ab6b9e6db4a762364b09ab0f8f005\nparent 844f20852a35cdec5ed0af6f55d05432aa991535\nauthor Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1789320034 +0530\ncommitter Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1789320034 +0530\n\nfeat(local-dev): one-command native dev stack (dev-up.sh / dev-down.sh)\n\nAddresses the platform review''s top contributor-friction item: cold-starting the\nplatform meant hand-launching six services in order with no launcher. dev-up.sh\nbrings them up natively (no Docker) in dependency order — catalog (Java+H2, no\nexternal DB), ingest, matter-management MFE, agent, Studio, Hub — each\nidempotent (a listening port is left alone) and behind a bounded health gate,\nlogging to platform/local-dev/.logs/. It bakes in SEED_REMOTES for the\nmatter-management remote so the Hub''s matter-* widgets resolve on load (the\n''Unknown widget'' issue won''t recur). dev-down.sh stops by port; both take an\noptional service-name filter. README documents ports, prereqs, and that\nStudio''s local authMode is left untouched.\n\nVerified: run against a partially-down stack, it cold-started the missing\nservices to all-healthy (6/6 200); detached processes survive the launcher exit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCAAdFiEE1eujchKuJhYER67YWqdl9Lsba5AFAmqm22MACgkQWqdl9Lsb\na5BjqgwAkQzo8yJoXAO7C1Qew9/G5sBuntlid/c0+gWGPO0OG7vx6mvsqzYZsqZc\ncOsPbbzn36ymUoh0YYWpYKMc5qNR9QiQ/KOAtu1XuDKTuj6p+Pal26MeAImg+7xk\nX5MiW9Ns883RNDeyUIm9adIyIdunvC7yCkixo3aetgvj6xopOwDrJMLfTohF4j7d\nV9vHNBGYQqcGzK60a2WouJHKeuzuavRP16eFFWH/R7DHJet8T9Lm4krixF47H1TF\na6W4N/i/AM/lkVsp1MqJHGR+jcDqrmBsTpTQoVBGwJ7ASJntRUEYWTKMEJJ