user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/2826f057f37afca6d37b03b2a4ba560dd6adc765/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T17:29:29Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T17:29:29Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"message":"fix(studio): components registry is exempt from the application filter\n\nComponents are the shared building blocks (the widget palette) every\napplication composes from, not app-owned artifacts — so the Components registry\nmust always list all of them, never scoped to one application. The application\nfilter now skips exempt kinds (APP_FILTER_EXEMPT_KINDS = {component}); a small\n''shared building blocks — not filtered by application'' hint shows on the count\nline when a filter is active there. Membership chips still render (they show\nwhich apps use a component), and every other category stays scoped.\n\nVerified live: with acme-workspace selected, Components stays 214 of 214 while\nForms is 1 of 18.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"15a0044254869ff75de7306a505af4e6409af5b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/15a0044254869ff75de7306a505af4e6409af5b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/2826f057f37afca6d37b03b2a4ba560dd6adc765","verification":{"payload":"tree 15a0044254869ff75de7306a505af4e6409af5b6\nparent 93fd37fccac2fb6012a05baa7d96774173f70afd\nauthor Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788370169 +0530\ncommitter Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788370169 +0530\n\nfix(studio): components registry is exempt from the application filter\n\nComponents are the shared building blocks (the widget palette) every\napplication composes from, not app-owned artifacts — so the Components registry\nmust always list all of them, never scoped to one application. The application\nfilter now skips exempt kinds (APP_FILTER_EXEMPT_KINDS = {component}); a small\n''shared building blocks — not filtered by application'' hint shows on the count\nline when a filter is active there. Membership chips still render (they show\nwhich apps use a component), and every other category stays scoped.\n\nVerified live: with acme-workspace selected, Components stays 214 of 214 while\nForms is 1 of 18.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCAAdFiEE1eujchKuJhYER67YWqdl9Lsba5AFAmqYXPkACgkQWqdl9Lsb\na5ApFgwAppN6Rt2w0kHqf0EWL4wVWSHey4Gjln7uEgexl3fkofoUCrK4BSdfIop1\nJFq6q9TNGfiK2Bp5/xY5U6IjyE1kax8VWG0YtFB1jdXNH/57Q4cYM48w3BVbya2z\ndiYshOzEIV1ZQXsUnXrdUzXPwgGbtqksVKaMIsPMHiNSTnXy7NOIRgBtYs7HWXRD\ndM4jhykMl4dwskWnCuk54CdPhomuMEjQGK97fQZx+k2bxb/A0DLPAeITtMpGZZZ/\nnUwhlmKSLyl8KC02jcMXOwLt/bAgDQB/2ZixRF488qnpqwSt0Rleub4ssG2fYsPc\nLyHf1Dh2aNWdQskKQ0ZjLFrdwfV2NG+xZlX8im2eTQwp7F6JQ3UX9p6yDHvlylS/\n4nSdxsfHfkSplLMNu0kO0TXn9iciPXEwmLI+gUsK5waaMwBoN7CqrNFk151pTZuo\nlT4m1Zjlc35qdOf5r7HXHulIIYEyPVZNmTEGqLFy/RfH6uKDOOn6ByFa0D4RFeuw\nBcMIBqtO\n=dGzT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T17:29:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/2826f057f37afca6d37b03b2a4ba560dd6adc765","node_id":"C_kwDOSNG7mtoAKDI4MjZmMDU3ZjM3YWZjYTZkMzdiMDNiMmE0YmE1NjBkZDZhZGM3NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/93fd37fccac2fb6012a05baa7d96774173f70afd","sha":"93fd37fccac2fb6012a05baa7d96774173f70afd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/93fd37fccac2fb6012a05baa7d96774173f70afd"}],"sha":"2826f057f37afca6d37b03b2a4ba560dd6adc765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/2826f057f37afca6d37b03b2a4ba560dd6adc765"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/93fd37fccac2fb6012a05baa7d96774173f70afd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T17:26:14Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T17:26:14Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"message":"feat(studio): app chips on workflow & experience lists + fix experience membership\n\nExtend the application-membership chips (and click-to-filter) to the bespoke\nworkflow and experiences lists, for parity with the generic category list.\n\nAlso fix membersOf(): experiences live in a SEPARATE store, so a page''s\nexperience reference resolves as ''unmet'' in the capability graph and the\nforward closure never recorded it — which silently made both the experience\nchips AND the experience application-filter match nothing. membersOf now\nrecords a referenced key even for leaves the graph doesn''t hold (experiences),\nwhile still only traversing into resolved capabilities.\n\nVerified live: workflow rows show their app chips; experiences now show\n◆ acme-workspace and filtering experiences by acme-workspace lists the four it\ncomposes. Studio typechecks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3cfd88d8ad10634500c7a5a741323cc2cc338adc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/3cfd88d8ad10634500c7a5a741323cc2cc338adc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/93fd37fccac2fb6012a05baa7d96774173f70afd","verification":{"payload":"tree 3cfd88d8ad10634500c7a5a741323cc2cc338adc\nparent 4250c0b0cb198358bbbcfd48b87a9e7eed2dbc06\nauthor Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788369974 +0530\ncommitter Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788369974 +0530\n\nfeat(studio): app chips on workflow & experience lists + fix experience membership\n\nExtend the application-membership chips (and click-to-filter) to the bespoke\nworkflow and experiences lists, for parity with the generic category list.\n\nAlso fix membersOf(): experiences live in a SEPARATE store, so a page''s\nexperience reference resolves as ''unmet'' in the capability graph and the\nforward closure never recorded it — which silently made both the experience\nchips AND the experience application-filter match nothing. membersOf now\nrecords a referenced key even for leaves the graph doesn''t hold (experiences),\nwhile still only traversing into resolved capabilities.\n\nVerified live: workflow rows show their app chips; experiences now show\n◆ acme-workspace and filtering experiences by acme-workspace lists the four it\ncomposes. Studio typechecks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCAAdFiEE1eujchKuJhYER67YWqdl9Lsba5AFAmqYXDcACgkQWqdl9Lsb\na5DH+wv/Z5/8XozLQx1ZyiaExSCYbP4ieie3xSDQP4v7jnlIOe/i3l8GTXmGvCaY\n/UU9Ngl7fTUFy+mjPLVpsaqg+h5208ce30ZszzGilMC/amhE7lSVqSVO+M8Zo7FB\n4n4ymIzJPQgZ7IBrEO9Q7FeOJqptYX9VXupyBdKiY1T1puF8qJuiYocfMuZR30vM\n66mPQqPiFBNPOY5fsBaa+Tg9eN609jUXe7m5KcfCqf7vT+zT1glIvOrkLgiTGOMd\n/HStFO0ENZ/rtz3vCGyVMd2cuWMCEkGLdU443ncfXFRt4VOluiKLykIqIzsBC4h1\nellcNkq6yu/QFpOIFrvOmkyYO8D7RDrajYSWoGW0IhY9rAqQnSfulcR5KaM7iVlO\n4GYplxqxzT2LppN2P5ZXn6bR4NLBsYPaLFrgZG0/adivZxjjdBdsaJ1GVNP/BwVu\nZQWMoIW23BsnSqre1nZ7aWvMXUv/cER7lckRERP4d3Xlq3vx3c4VpH5laMeQEnon\nkKb3T6Bl\n=vUiv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T17:26:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/r