wing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/e91cf191fe8ff2915dab9a086d3c9880b8d9728b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:32:19Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:32:19Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"message":"feat(studio): category indicators + correct jump links in the copilot rail\n\nThe rail now lists the capabilities the copilot drafted/edited this session,\neach tagged with its category (a chip: Form, Prompt, …) and an honest action\nlink: ''Open in the <kind> designer'' for kinds that have a rich designer, and\n''Go to <Category>'' (the category list) for kinds that don''t — replacing the old\nsingle button that always said ''Open in designer'' even for kinds without one.\nNewest-first, deduped by id, last 6. Recents come from a shared recentDrafts\nsignal the authoring tools push to on create/update.\n\nVerified live: a form shows ''Form · Open in the form designer'', a prompt shows\n''Prompt · Go to Prompt''.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f70bb404cb6f3748afadd842932805d6bf364778","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/f70bb404cb6f3748afadd842932805d6bf364778"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/e91cf191fe8ff2915dab9a086d3c9880b8d9728b","verification":{"payload":"tree f70bb404cb6f3748afadd842932805d6bf364778\nparent ef5d5b17de8f9510f765acfc6c7e8cfa0263d6c2\nauthor Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788366739 +0530\ncommitter Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788366739 +0530\n\nfeat(studio): category indicators + correct jump links in the copilot rail\n\nThe rail now lists the capabilities the copilot drafted/edited this session,\neach tagged with its category (a chip: Form, Prompt, …) and an honest action\nlink: ''Open in the <kind> designer'' for kinds that have a rich designer, and\n''Go to <Category>'' (the category list) for kinds that don''t — replacing the old\nsingle button that always said ''Open in designer'' even for kinds without one.\nNewest-first, deduped by id, last 6. Recents come from a shared recentDrafts\nsignal the authoring tools push to on create/update.\n\nVerified live: a form shows ''Form · Open in the form designer'', a prompt shows\n''Prompt · Go to Prompt''.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCAAdFiEE1eujchKuJhYER67YWqdl9Lsba5AFAmqYT5MACgkQWqdl9Lsb\na5ANOQwAzfpka4CNZ6eyFcfoeafhyeu9LfXB6zCovpWBqI9rKRamrlT+vMCARy1C\nixUhePeUzJUOKzRuJkkqWQNatNrpNMjoQXrA3EMteeG+Z80OLr6kLTGL5pCMQBMt\nAy5gRfc4WcZ9oJR1BgafwIMfSz8fbWTSaemYftc/pRFokZlxsuE2w370///PTiAk\n++JunbRuLpmpRXMMYNCyBDT8xhwNurUR4qzJzbrQlzzLimsuluwDWzSNAckIiEh9\nRN7rYc2Lu1KpP4gqZ8jHTEuQoAQt1riwLwDjos3MneuMPso76CJSTswF4hY7SyfJ\nCWDOazwHsP/OrW7Lk0lYSd8PMTGwbAO9bS+6AO1GHFbzn2qgcS3fNNrDMNgetplK\nHHRkhJaXfJSHR9e4ywt7eT0XETP+GEKewM40//XCvynq8edv+A0QFIZq6yGnDxrr\nqwKorMhM6cLuEl27yUds0ZtHqbm0CW/cbRA8shoaP8hl2DkGQHZWRh6z0rzfeVVk\ncktpqcpn\n=limX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T16:32:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/e91cf191fe8ff2915dab9a086d3c9880b8d9728b","node_id":"C_kwDOSNG7mtoAKGU5MWNmMTkxZmU4ZmYyOTE1ZGFiOWEwODZkM2M5ODgwYjhkOTcyOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/ef5d5b17de8f9510f765acfc6c7e8cfa0263d6c2","sha":"ef5d5b17de8f9510f765acfc6c7e8cfa0263d6c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/ef5d5b17de8f9510f765acfc6c7e8cfa0263d6c2"}],"sha":"e91cf191fe8ff2915dab9a086d3c9880b8d9728b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/e91cf191fe8ff2915dab9a086d3c9880b8d9728b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/ef5d5b17de8f9510f765acfc6c7e8cfa0263d6c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:26:03Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:26:03Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"message":"fix(studio): copilot works on the open designer; live-refresh across all kinds\n\nThree issues when authoring with the copilot:\n\n1. Creating/opening another capability didn''t update the designer. Angular\n   REUSES a designer component across /<kind>s/:id/design → :otherId/design\n   (only the param changes), but every designer loaded once in its constructor,\n   so it kept showing the previous capability. Fixed: load reactively on the\n   routed id.\n\n2. A field/step the copilot added to the OPEN capability didn''t appear — the\n   copilot writes the catalog out-of-band while the designer holds its own\n   in-memory state, and Studio has no live catalog stream. Fixed: the copilot\n   records each create/update (lastMutation), and an open designer live-reloads\n   when its own capability changes (skipping when the author has unsaved edits,\n   so their work isn''t clobbered). Also added getActiveCapability so the copilot\n   can resolve ''this''/''the open form'' to the capability in the designer instead\n   of only ones it created earlier in the chat.\n\n3. Both fixes are shared via wireDesignerLiveSync and applied to ALL designers\n   (form, workflow, decision, page, application, theme) — not just forms — so\n   every category behaves the same.\n\nVerified live (Gemini): with a form open, ''add a phone field to this form'' →\nthe open designer went Rating → Rating,Phone in ~4.5s with no manual refresh;\nand ''create a new form …'' redirected to the new form showing its fields (not\nstale). Studio typechecks; copilot spec updated (5 tools).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"382e083d6c3f841e49f3f7827c8bea772b123ee4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/382e083d6c3f841e49f3f7827c8bea772b123ee4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/ef5d5b17de8f9510f765acfc6c7e8cfa0263d6c2","verification":{"payload":"tree 382e083d6c3f841e49f3f7827c8bea772b123ee4\nparent 1932e1f577f60aeb68083253bba3223df336bfcc\nauthor Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788366363 +0530\ncommitter Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788366363 +0530\n\nfix(studio): copilot works on the open designer; live-refresh across all kinds\n\nThree issues when authoring with the copilot:\n\n1. Creating/opening another capability didn''t update the designer. Angular\n   REUSES a designer component across /<kind>s/:id/design → :otherId/design\n   (only the param changes), but every designer loaded once in its constructor,\n   so it kept showing the previous capability. Fixed: load reactively on the\n   routed id.\n\n2. A field/step the copilot added to the OPEN capability didn''t appear — the\n   copilot writes the catalog out-of-band while the designer holds its own\n   in-memory state, and Studio has no live catalog stream. Fixed: the copilot\n   records each create/update (lastMutation), and an open designer live-reloads\n   when its own capability changes (skipping when the author has unsaved edits,\n   so their work isn''t clobbered). Also added getActiveCapability so the copilot\n   can resolve ''this''/''the open form'' to the capability in the designer instead\n   of only ones it created earlier in the chat.\n\n3. Both fixes are shared via wireDesignerLiveSync and applied to ALL designers\n   (form, workflow, decision, page, application, theme) — not just forms — so\n   every category behaves the same.\n\nVerified live (Gemini): with a form open, ''add a phone field to this form'' →\nthe open designer went Rating → Rating,Phone in ~4.5s with no manual refresh;\nand ''create a new form …'' redirected to the new form showing its fields (not\nstale). Studio typechecks; copilot spec updated (5 tools).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCAAdFiEE1eujchKuJhYER67YWqdl9Lsba5AFAmqYThwACgkQWqdl9Lsb\na5AKHwv+JGr89dAxDNZphQj1zZmvpmC2g1jgXIcN5ablDJLE/M/2eP8xnCSs42mx\np6sxXVt4kbIOZihA9lRiO7R4KTdX5KsU/nBb9ksfwajlh9X3CF4egCa2GXYNcytm\nTivdhbGgPi8VggeU69xN2fW9SgToPnr1P3JS4rQS2t4i29yA6Op4EcYo/fQUNG6S\nKPTY86pRpi9B+W1vFhxs20gUt0H51SHJrDEQ1FUmTXO7RplEJ9vY15boz5fRXbwf\nsHLolpKB38/Zj0b3HUrGt/TPwrCEZ1MlMkv68yuUADunyz1WlLgLz4HpMwqWeDIj\nRPsA+KWBXoun+G2hY+9ZSTACoFESr5vw6gzufKMK/HYlTt4Rbx1KTDjOTTwjQmfV\nJGrH3CEkm+A47ubjlp67IQtW+Y7XiaesBOa2/Thh+xkLTGQByBLxK9L/otSVPYtY\n0bJCBXcqY0bhmyPzoj9ifH0rPnyde0kZCvtFDnmr0dd3pgbwX3TRVclvYeWrucJU\njuInuRZ5\n=yt41\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T16:26:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/ef5d5b17de8f9510f765acfc6c7e8cfa0263d6c2","node_id":"C_kwDOSNG7mtoAKGVmNWQ1YjE3ZGU4Zjk1MTBmNzY1YWNmYzZjN2U4Y2ZhMDI2M2Q2YzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/1932e1f577f60aeb68083253bba3223df336bfcc","sha":"1932e1f577f60aeb68083253bba3223df336bfcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/1932e1f577f60aeb68083253bba3223df336bfcc"}],"sha":"ef5d5b17de8f9510f765acfc6c7e8cfa0263d6c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/ef5d5b17de8f9510f765acfc6c7e8cfa0263d6c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/1932e1f577f60aeb68083253bba3223df336bfcc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:13:20Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:13:20Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"message":"ci(schematics): guard that release workflows cover every snapshot input\n\nThe platform + examples schematics packages publish a build-time snapshot of\nthe repo, triggered by a hand-maintained on.push.paths allow-list in each\nrelease workflow. If a snapshot input dir/file is added but the workflow paths\naren''t updated to match, a change there silently stops republishing and the\npublished schematic goes stale — exactly the ''always latest codebase'' promise\nwe don''t want to break.\n\nMake the snapshot inputs a single source of truth (snapshot-inputs.mjs per\npackage, imported by populate-templates.mjs) and add scripts/\ncheck-schematics-release-paths.mjs, which asserts each release workflow''s paths\ncover every input (topDirs -> <dir>/**, topFiles, tsconfig*.json). Wired into\nthe ci.yml lib-version-guard job so drift fails the PR. Both packages pass\ntoday (platform 11 inputs, examples 1); verified the guard also fails on an\ninjected missing path. Platform + examples builds still green after the refactor.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"55865853c73ecb45f36bea838a98461f9d7334a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/55865853c73ecb45f36bea838a98461f9d7334a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/1932e1f577f60aeb68083253bba3223df336bfcc","verification":{"payload":"tree 55865853c73ecb45f36bea838a98461f9d7334a7\nparent 83f705348ce953cc1e6c33b5d6f3f94e8fc6f0e8\nauthor Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788347600 +0530\ncommitter Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788347600 +0530\n\nci(schematics): guard that release workflows cover every snapshot input\n\nThe platform + examples schematics packages publish a build-time snapshot of\nthe repo, triggered by a hand-maintained on.push.paths allow-list in each\nrelease workflow. If a snapshot input dir/file is added but the workflow paths\naren''t updated to match, a change there silently stops republishing and the\npublished schematic goes stale — exactly the ''always latest codebase'' promise\nwe don''t want to break.\n\nMake the snapshot inputs a single source of truth (snapshot-inputs.mjs per\npackage, imported by populate-templates.mjs) and add scripts/\ncheck-schematics-release-paths.mjs, which asserts each release workflow''s paths\ncover every input (topDirs -> <dir>/**, topFiles, tsconfig*.json). Wired into\nthe ci.yml lib-version-guard job so drift fails the PR. Both packages pass\ntoday (platform 11 inputs, examples 1); verified the guard also fails on an\ninjected missing path. Platform + examples builds still green after the refactor.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCAAdFiEE1eujchKuJhYER67YWqdl9Lsba5AFAmqYBNcACgkQWqdl9Lsb\na5DVEAv/fBaItopQSMNr/PwUPLl5Sw4pc7wkhQtDw4i27gRXUf939/eOZdDKwglU\neIXueET8m3NJigySWnspSV444fBr48TZrHTPStTb/RyHw0O09LMd2HQsGGvRB4Fi\nT30zALtzOsT6z8McUg3FPg9Alh+VvkiYbLmH+IkDWBBa8Low/Q73QJWschUda/Nw\ncSaijq3Np6cgzSZ52tAnr/TRAwI8I5zbo+MmvR+H5MlLkbQOADSf+uAOoLwhw3oZ\nFIFft4vtatBX0fa1KGEyZPeLv32ZdaE3UbMgsdo/q8PKmvIWfKgDiRjBm9UNKujD\nBa2mQXKX0OgirmBkZrxoG+C2pbKLcEvix/Z/SfxX8hprEpuMP+SoJYy6jiy1q2UA\nAQgzqjQDmOZLnIU3UHDJfNL1zD2oSP2wgX8GNVenDxz5Q2ofz7cVK+RCIMDWjU+j\njTYfBnv/3NJZB+0jXC7bZLitjASGRqg8YUsK0iV06VKnR80/FmXtYUlAgy1UY0Yp\neGZipwv9\n=QXa4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T11:13:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/1932e1f577f60aeb68083253bba3223df336bfcc","node_id":"C_kwDOSNG7mtoAKDE5MzJlMWY1NzdmNjBhZWI2ODA4MzI1M2JiYTMyMjNkZjMzNmJmY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/83f705348ce953cc1e6c33b5d6f3f94e8fc6f0e8","sha":"83f705348ce953cc1e6c33b5d6f3f94e8fc6f0e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/83f705348ce953cc1e6c33b5d6f3f94e8fc6f0e8"}],"sha":"1932e1f577f60aeb68083253bba3223df336bfcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/1932e1f577f60aeb68083253bba3223df336bfcc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/83f705348ce953cc1e6c33b5d6f3f94e8fc6f0e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T12:11:34Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T12:11:34Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"message":"feat(catalog-server): emit capability kind on mutation events\n\nShip the changed capability''s kind on the SSE mutation event (create/update/\ndelete) so a client can re-hydrate ONLY the source that owns that kind with no\nfollow-up lookup — the server-side completion of the client''s targeted\nre-hydrate. kind is not tenant-sensitive, so it stays RLS-safe (we still never\nship the full row). The lib client already reads m.kind (skips its own lookup\nwhen present, and now targets deletes too), so this is purely additive and\nactivates on the next catalog-server restart/deploy.\n\n- CatalogMutationEvent gains optional kind.\n- create/update/delete publish sites set it (create already carried it in\n  summary; update/delete now expose it top-level).\n- Test: subscribe to the bus, create→update→delete, assert each event''s kind.\n  Full events + capabilities suites green (18/18).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a2b8eb067b2c2585dc22696c143ea5a5f165c63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/0a2b8eb067b2c2585dc22696c143ea5a5f165c63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/83f705348ce953cc1e6c33b5d6f3f94e8fc6f0e8","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a2b8eb067b2c2585dc22696c143ea5a5f165c63\nparent d32aed26e5f9fd8711600484f1615c6978002c76\nauthor Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788264694 +0530\ncommitter Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788264694 +0530\n\nfeat(catalog-server): emit capability kind on mutation events\n\nShip the changed capability''s kind on the SSE mutation event (create/update/\ndelete) so a client can re-hydrate ONLY the source that owns that kind with no\nfollow-up lookup — the server-side completion of the client''s targeted\nre-hydrate. kind is not tenant-sensitive, so it stays RLS-safe (we still never\nship the full row). The lib client already reads m.kind (skips its own lookup\nwhen present, and now targets deletes too), so this is purely additive and\nactivates on the next catalog-server restart/deploy.\n\n- CatalogMutationEvent gains optional kind.\n- create/update/delete publish sites set it (create already carried it in\n  summary; update/delete now expose it top-level).\n- Test: subscribe to the bus, create→update→delete, assert each event''s kind.\n  Full events + capabilities suites green (18/18).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCAAdFiEE1eujchKuJhYER67YWqdl9Lsba5AFAmqWwPcACgkQWqdl9Lsb\na5AVQAv/SyYrFQPhQVhvIfhCi0yZD/VBEpqbDcw2n371yqBZhMTORPCmrLLYdPkm\nmjuBAKfiMR940/xVISbRt0Hspga/w6bmur9awz9n/xMdtvLbfG42yed+3NxVN96U\nQ5SViOBoCCoEGRTOniG4dghfKkUIxF/RDmNGMeBkUs5N0VaPBLxvUK9VSjQxoPAc\n22y1rTBfmhtcR4JHJV2BzGFSMaIpxB9erffSjlzRRD4W6uwVYRVXMV+Wd7Zi1/fB\n3MLDaUtmXVSJEBSxx65cBjTl7fsQAQAAQ1B0i4HZd4OHdalIuKyiuWylb+NnNZFY\ns/uD0tGoUIV9AsHZ4pNHqyZ0yPYeZnUhUwG0IMaDoEqL/Ek6fkFh+w5aIQnsWgOO\nSqqqK6k+A0+qAYgrWJpJhvojJyer0QyI4MOfbOJyRBF1I2c0ZB4ZtqWRIQ08DbV/\nXSvIiXNVc0kZADGE42zUQ5F/L2XRiPfZYCoGbyYRMv/yPS3hloqxD/sTZOg8psr7\nb35Q23+7\n=878l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T12:11:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/83f705348ce953cc1e6c33b5d6f3f94e8fc6f0e8","node_id":"C_kwDOSNG7mtoAKDgzZjcwNTM0OGNlOTUzY2MxZTZjMzNiNWQ2ZjNmOTRlOGZjNmYwZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/d32aed26e5f9fd8711600484f1615c6978002c76","sha":"d32aed26e5f9fd8711600484f1615c6978002c76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/d32aed26e5f9fd8711600484f1615c6978002c76"}],"sha":"83f705348ce953cc1e6c33b5d6f3f94e8fc6f0e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/83f705348ce953cc1e6c33b5d6f3f94e8fc6f0e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/d32aed26e5f9fd8711600484f1615c6978002c76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T09:29:31Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T09:29:31Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"message":"perf(catalog): targeted SSE re-hydrate — resolve kind, refresh only the affected source\n\nBefore: any capability edit fanned out to every capability source, so a single\nform save triggered ~13 full listByKind() re-fetches (one per kind) even though\n12 were unaffected. The service''s SSE event carries entityType + entityId +\noperation but NO kind, so a listener couldn''t tell what changed.\n\nNow CatalogClient resolves the changed capability''s kind CLIENT-SIDE from its\nentityId (one deduped GET /capabilities/{id}) before fanning out an enriched\nevent, and sources register via onCapabilityKind(kind, cb) so only the matching\nsource re-hydrates. A single edit becomes 1 kind lookup + 1 targeted refresh\ninstead of 13. Deletes / missing id / lookup failure fan out with kind\nundefined → listeners broad-refresh (safe fallback, so a removed row still\nleaves its registry). Experience mutations keep their own listener.\n\n- capabilityMutationMatches(m, kind) — pure, exported, unit-tested (match /\n  skip-other-kind / broad-on-unknown / never-on-experience).\n- All 12 capability sources (form, workflow, datasource, tool, prompt, skill,\n  navigation, validation, decision, theme, page, application) migrated;\n  application also keeps an experience listener.\n\nVerified: 4 predicate specs + full suite green; live server→client proof —\na form create resolved kind=form and a decision create resolved kind=decision\nfrom their entityIds against the running :8081 catalog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f1eac056da582687443481d7f396cb6ed4feb6bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/f1eac056da582687443481d7f396cb6ed4feb6bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/d32aed26e5f9fd8711600484f1615c6978002c76","verification":{"payload":"tree f1eac056da582687443481d7f396cb6ed4feb6bd\nparent ac37111307364e59c4c18fc078783be277ee1f59\nauthor Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788254971 +0530\ncommitter Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788254971 +0530\n\nperf(catalog): targeted SSE re-hydrate — resolve kind, refresh only the affected source\n\nBefore: any capability edit fanned out to every capability source, so a single\nform save triggered ~13 full listByKind() re-fetches (one per kind) even though\n12 were unaffected. The service''s SSE event carries entityType + entityId +\noperation but NO kind, so a listener couldn''t tell what changed.\n\nNow CatalogClient resolves the changed capability''s kind CLIENT-SIDE from its\nentityId (one deduped GET /capabilities/{id}) before fanning out an enriched\nevent, and sources register via onCapabilityKind(kind, cb) so only the matching\nsource re-hydrates. A single edit becomes 1 kind lookup + 1 targeted refresh\ninstead of 13. Deletes / missing id / lookup failure fan out with kind\nundefined → listeners broad-refresh (safe fallback, so a removed row still\nleaves its registry). Experience mutations keep their own listener.\n\n- capabilityMutationMatches(m, kind) — pure, exported, unit-tested (match /\n  skip-other-kind / broad-on-unknown / never-on-experience).\n- All 12 capability sources (form, workflow, datasource, tool, prompt, skill,\n  navigation, validation, decision, theme, page, application) migrated;\n  application also keeps an experience listener.\n\nVerified: 4 predicate specs + full suite green; live server→client proof —\na form create resolved kind=form and a decision create resolved kind=decision\nfrom their entityIds against the running :8081 catalog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCAAdFiEE1eujchKuJhYER67YWqdl9Lsba5AFAmqWmv0ACgkQWqdl9Lsb\na5D0CAwAlzUqc1Mgtt9wLWjgC9QKsMQMQHSwFnzZEAyKQA7VFeHoWSh1wOI7NySs\nrDHN2gTdWk5crEu692yF45GVyGoU8Zjc8xMYTYb5xJtRoUty3zuxQm/aP2yx/Dy6\nMK4N6Rtp7RNExq0cC8xhWHkEtokqj3MSXBwGLLGzwNDFuHKfir8NPiyGawZQ1kMe\nYQ9cc1HIfyDsNEZSESbnFIF1WWVSk8X/77A215WGa4eyo5ALExrIqziN+Gh2nmrQ\n10HMol9cz0nVstgSHVnA829nJTvZqF8/W8Ej8DEGUFDWVYYOlYC/O+tkdXvAngjU\nGNta11TIbZ3xRBcEQRqlen42ETwTee9f6t12Vb8/o6eAdRWNvTVK0zvJfCXxcoLN\n9mrWXRJq3ut6ga1qICBIu+ed29DEeH6WGn+dkL3fgMCDiDa6ZAPN4MUuPsCXuSD6\nbdEgFmxhDAKspx0HHbTOqU/oouVssJ7x6Se4uARDsshLDHJ35Mc1OiuiqPIiyT6/\nggUCP6pK\n=O2tR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T09:29:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ