assakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/ac37111307364e59c4c18fc078783be277ee1f59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T09:10:42Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T09:10:42Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"message":"feat(studio): copilot workflow refine-in-place — chain-safe step edits\n\nupdateDraftCapability already replaces top-level body keys, but its guidance\nwas form-centric. Add workflow-specific guidance (tool description + authoring\nspecialist prompt): to add/remove/reorder a step, send the ENTIRE steps array\nin final order and keep the next-chain valid — re-point next on the neighbours\nof any inserted/removed step, last step''s next is null. Also harden the server\nprompt so a natural ''add X to the Y workflow'' is treated as a REFINE of the\nexisting capability (getCapability by name+kind → updateDraftCapability), not a\nnew-capability create.\n\nVerified live (Gemini): inserting a manager-approval step between documents and\nreview yields details→documents→manager-approval→review→(end) — neighbours\nre-pointed, one terminal, all steps reachable — from natural phrasing, ~6s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cdecf95c7d2d44183b94d7f3e6c98e5914653201","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/cdecf95c7d2d44183b94d7f3e6c98e5914653201"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/ac37111307364e59c4c18fc078783be277ee1f59","verification":{"payload":"tree cdecf95c7d2d44183b94d7f3e6c98e5914653201\nparent ea0550bdc826c6086ce4bd6a4eb06834464a00b1\nauthor Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788253842 +0530\ncommitter Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788253842 +0530\n\nfeat(studio): copilot workflow refine-in-place — chain-safe step edits\n\nupdateDraftCapability already replaces top-level body keys, but its guidance\nwas form-centric. Add workflow-specific guidance (tool description + authoring\nspecialist prompt): to add/remove/reorder a step, send the ENTIRE steps array\nin final order and keep the next-chain valid — re-point next on the neighbours\nof any inserted/removed step, last step''s next is null. Also harden the server\nprompt so a natural ''add X to the Y workflow'' is treated as a REFINE of the\nexisting capability (getCapability by name+kind → updateDraftCapability), not a\nnew-capability create.\n\nVerified live (Gemini): inserting a manager-approval step between documents and\nreview yields details→documents→manager-approval→review→(end) — neighbours\nre-pointed, one terminal, all steps reachable — from natural phrasing, ~6s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCAAdFiEE1eujchKuJhYER67YWqdl9Lsba5AFAmqWlpMACgkQWqdl9Lsb\na5CLUAv8Df9QVWUFxb2zqbKQs2BfjA/wAyV2z1duztV1ukwWGWAv57VRRlOLa+mU\nUlzXgKt08zDZFU5qmYv9nU/s3QhUs9mydesoV7VCRzOTlAfTGub7eIDs9IR6LSBd\nuhLJ3+h5XPZT5vyuztNl7UvZxrZB/5kFI4MMXcRMARY2DJkvbIaNnb/Jy/O0voK8\naq9iN4CqpVTlKmcgda1WxV3ntNbRff2hmx19KIo79T4AdcvC6thYq8gjJNF8CTaj\njwXotVGUiSLqGOJ+If3bepInoUHes9NciBEYeE43GQGIjJS2H58+FvSXS9zom1N/\n5DlBs6B0k9oxVIt5yRS/wEzCwMQfCOmWQVtkhBjP7hR/GbvdibjY1LQpOPrBvVDA\n9wuGyiSBpHjWa4OErgXu1/OTBAgSKSeGJP0gS39fQgIPjEr9g2Cqs4Gy7NEMXAaa\n7DarGRyPvCxOR1FU7Jg5CVWckzlWccVrXbtLUptx36elVjePNVzCBoTTNEjZLjk7\n0MLNcEbX\n=y3hC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T09:11:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/ac37111307364e59c4c18fc078783be277ee1f59","node_id":"C_kwDOSNG7mtoAKGFjMzcxMTEzMDczNjRlNTljNGMxOGZjMDc4NzgzYmUyNzdlZTFmNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/ea0550bdc826c6086ce4bd6a4eb06834464a00b1","sha":"ea0550bdc826c6086ce4bd6a4eb06834464a00b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/ea0550bdc826c6086ce4bd6a4eb06834464a00b1"}],"sha":"ac37111307364e59c4c18fc078783be277ee1f59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/ac37111307364e59c4c18fc078783be277ee1f59"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/ea0550bdc826c6086ce4bd6a4eb06834464a00b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T19:49:06Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T19:49:06Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"Sahas Sakhare"},"message":"feat(catalog): on-demand federated component loading from catalog rows\n\nClose the ingest→render loop: the component-ingest service registers one\nkind:''component'' catalog row per discovered component, each self-describing\n(remoteName + manifestUrl + exposedModule). CatalogComponentSource reads that\nand loads the remote LAZILY the first time a component surface needs it, then\nhands off to the host ComponentRegistry (which <mvk-widget-container> resolves\nby name). Complements the eager MFE-registry discovery in provideCatalogRuntime\n— here the catalog row itself is the source of truth, so a component renders\neven when it isn''t in the host''s configured registry env, and only remotes a\npage actually references are fetched (not all ~200 ingested ones).\n\n- CatalogComponentSource.ensure(name): registry hit → ''ready''; preview-only /\n  unknown row → ''not-federated''; else load the remote (deduped per remoteName,\n  failures not cached so a reload retries) via loadRemoteCapabilities.\n- The federation loader is injectable (CATALOG_REMOTE_LOADER) with a\n  Native-Federation default — bundler-agnostic + unit-testable, matching the\n  loader seam on loadRemoteCapabilities.\n- surface-host gates the ''component'' case on resolution state (loading / ready\n  / could-not-load) via an effect that flips to ready the moment the remote\n  registers the widget (ComponentRegistry.get is signal-reactive).\n- Wire catalog secondary-entry specs into the agentic-ui test target (they were\n  outside sourceRoot and never ran): +6 CatalogComponentSource tests and the\n  pre-existing 13 catalog-form-compile tests now execute. Suite: 1154 green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b5924712a2f809fbc1710d1fdeb1bda224face05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/b5924712a2f809fbc1710d1fdeb1bda224face05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/ea0550bdc826c6086ce4bd6a4eb06834464a00b1","verification":{"payload":"tree b5924712a2f809fbc1710d1fdeb1bda224face05\nparent 5af5b9cf17a361346c83efc2f5d31410fcb58abc\nauthor Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788205746 +0530\ncommitter Sahas Sakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1788205746 +0530\n\nfeat(catalog): on-demand federated component loading from catalog rows\n\nClose the ingest→render loop: the component-ingest service registers one\nkind:''component'' catalog row per discovered component, each self-describing\n(remoteName + manifestUrl + exposedModule). CatalogComponentSource reads that\nand loads the remote LAZILY the first time a component surface needs it, then\nhands off to the host ComponentRegistry (which <mvk-widget-container> resolves\nby name). Complements the eager MFE-registry discovery in provideCatalogRuntime\n— here the catalog row itself is the source of truth, so a component renders\neven when it isn''t in the host''s configured registry env, and only remotes a\npage actually references are fetched (not all ~200 ingested ones).\n\n- CatalogComponentSource.ensure(name): registry hit → ''ready''; preview-only /\n  unknown row → ''not-federated''; else load the remote (deduped per remoteName,\n  failures not cached so a reload retries) via loadRemoteCapabilities.\n- The federation loader is injectable (CATALOG_REMOTE_LOADER) with a\n  Native-Federation default — bundler-agnostic + unit-testable, matching the\n  loader seam on loadRemoteCapabilities.\n- surface-host gates the ''component'' case on resolution state (loading / ready\n  / could-not-load) via an effect that flips to ready the moment the remote\n  registers the widget (ComponentRegistry.get is signal-reactive).\n- Wire catalog secondary-entry specs into the agentic-ui test target (they were\n  outside sourceRoot and never ran): +6 CatalogComponentSource tests and the\n  pre-existing 13 catalog-form-compile tests now execute. Suite: 1154 green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCAAdFiEE1eujchKuJhYER67YWqdl9Lsba5AFAmqV2rMACgkQWqdl9Lsb\na5DP+wv/fKOEzXonnMJXCImo2JjZsaz7KgoaDXjugY1RxrUUsd7BFNm1YA8Ak/Re\nqCX0iPfNRoRefqoJ+xNxY9mgO7uTXQXAPKvBUAVJSET+dhKgRgNIx1mdX8HI7TBU\ntnLwo5IFHS4EDXA2xWymGhzq9DsWQyMr6/JOh5VoshJOXNrYYqcjmYXP22xX4KHX\n3BWsx04Jsrfvgwqs0lvlJFCt/c9C3KLMoqhi8SPX/E+GgTJ8PljDh5B1WYZYxmZq\njuvEXktN/gnjhJiRShxHT2/ODpJrl8aIKWF3ljZDY/qwfgqOJxN9wGHe7CmWbgRY\nuyYjGcRU7dXCS0HqaWsRndk1JqDKT6erAmtMHEeA3w55ZHD7OsH1Y/TEp/6o4Rfq\nVboaJ+qyYut1Xc8kcsaw1rw4VuGjyqfDEoGrY9p+0TGjmOk2ZVhrtppaLjI+QWCb\nWDlX70hZhm94/sM/v8+Wt2EOE0fuemmelwGQij5g9UrElLcVzpu7mZ+3Ma2TOD4c\nZhePSqjY\n=VPXt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T19:49:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https