estructive variant retints the\nfilled button''s primary → --danger. Overlays are the adoption category the\npolicy assigns to Material. ConfirmService.ask() returns a Promise, dropping into\nboth the async remove flow and the CanDeactivate guard.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0287f7fa7a1e116d23c058e08320426725130c01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/0287f7fa7a1e116d23c058e08320426725130c01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/515a7219c94fb42c8ef2398b76329c9060b5c5f6","verification":{"payload":"tree 0287f7fa7a1e116d23c058e08320426725130c01\nparent 67e3b887a04a34acc4c641f63285f778454d9229\nauthor sahassakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1787474785 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787474785 +0530\n\nfeat(studio): themed MatDialog confirm — first Material component adoption (#61)\n\nReplace the two native confirm() calls (remove-remote destructive action + the\nunsaved-changes route guard) with a reusable ConfirmService + Material\nConfirmDialogComponent. First real component from the Material foundation: the\ndialog reads the M3 system tokens remapped to Studio tokens, so it matches the\nStudio in both themes with no extra styling; the destructive variant retints the\nfilled button''s primary → --danger. Overlays are the adoption category the\npolicy assigns to Material. ConfirmService.ask() returns a Promise, dropping into\nboth the async remove flow and the CanDeactivate guard.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqirNhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM2wQAC+djv3eGXIe4G7mjTxAcRBS\n8ZHUfYB3TvRXVcemUCwu0ot1JekTB7l6ETayO0Qfkxosti0uKNr76k5ozpNNgTaJ\ne7uGrqRhez3A/BICVqXR6PBEn1R5qIbNE8/vJR2cShnZo9kB33JtqQHBdFlBd/Ml\nb2YwWGLnFh3LCYQtK1PAdcQLD8sTn4CLpkDkV53u14gk5a/JATpOW6m4RT6LlvB0\nXYLJtFB8++Fq1gtruFL8BHVgjrnTL1AulT4LawmrV1xHGlSaUCB6FEuD11fZuVKx\ndLhHxrEdBQNaIbbZ7a