agentic-ui/commits/515a7219c94fb42c8ef2398b76329c9060b5c5f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/67e3b887a04a34acc4c641f63285f778454d9229/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T08:26:41Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"sahassakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T08:26:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(studio): CDK drag-drop + undo/redo in the Workflow Designer (Phase 1) (#60)\n\nCompletes the canvas trilogy: Workflow Designer''s native HTML5 drag → CDK, grip\nas cdkDragHandle so step inputs/decision controls stay interactive, palette\ncomponents drag in as steps (copy), steps reorder within the canvas. Structural\nundo/redo over steps() (add/move/remove, not per-keystroke) with ↶/↷ + ⌘Z / ⌘⇧Z.\nPage, Form and Workflow designers now share one accessible drag+undo pattern.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"15d9f983608dccfd1b83d88380593d955ca94260","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/15d9f983608dccfd1b83d88380593d955ca94260"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/67e3b887a04a34acc4c641f63285f778454d9229","verification":{"payload":"tree 15d9f983608dccfd1b83d88380593d955ca94260\nparent fb28471dd33872fbc4db6bf523f734e2cfa1ffc4\nauthor sahassakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1787473601 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787473601 +0530\n\nfeat(studio): CDK drag-drop + undo/redo in the Workflow Designer (Phase 1) (#60)\n\nCompletes the canvas trilogy: Workflow Designer''s native HTML5 drag → CDK, grip\nas cdkDragHandle so step inputs/decision controls stay interactive, palette\ncomponents drag in as steps (copy), steps reorder within the canvas. Structural\nundo/redo over steps() (add/move/remove, not per-keystroke) with ↶/↷ + ⌘Z / ⌘⇧Z.\nPage, Form and Workflow designers now share one accessible drag+undo pattern.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiq7BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA23AQACpglxXjYjQfUoZDeGSKhidA\nFwkvDXI+jbBXxpdeA9VLdE9o8dI6/0P8zdmWDOKs1549/MwavDcqNhnBLY6M1n+W\nR52I32jGXO77P8dSQxm2LDuePQUxFHQflUkZX6HRJEE/trLhd/HidF6j/zheD2MJ\nzxScbxcrvAOYPlModLfCT5fyVhvTzVjY8mR/apw0ucm/GYnMbl4F66fXQMI63G2g\nnhGh3IEz0b1VyNUGZF368wTnRtcTQ5TVzx32XIW7HIeQN2pSU3OIIkULE3mzVelY\nvboNl5fmW0lqh3xKxNoQCQelE+c1i+44WAcc0rmPLR3UZ4INVF6KkYP01jUT4kB7\nla0Jf3YcVtztQlCTR0laP2v6x7I/bqfQGhUcm/iiQySpRd2h9VbARgMJtWPwjETy\nmdhhhGSBw/DqyKQb9VUy6HVegYSVJe79+GY2EcTCG7DJ70Ri1In9h/edhdJ717jg\n+TDwuMA7gpmhBk9fzcZRdC0wdKxjWMFQIc9PSlKj05LJwqHKvJVYMaW4rCc9/PfO\nrICTLGNHdZgckZFTC+yMZpCa7jD/i2IqbTJmyVZGLEQNCHF3NaxPUeSCBRpvOtDT\nMmPDFnWVPe5xx7F2hr4cy2i97YroLgbbp1a9SyB9KdX3G4rpHMUs2HEAuM4JOMXZ\nW/hvw40QDUJ25LBRYlMj\n=LY2I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T08:26:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/67e3b887a04a34acc4c641f63285f778454d9229","node_id":"C_kwDOSNG7mtoAKDY3ZTNiODg3YTA0YTM0YWNjNGM2NDFmNjMyODVmNzc4NDU0ZDkyMjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/fb28471dd33872fbc4db6bf523f734e2cfa1ffc4","sha":"fb28471dd33872fbc4db6bf523f734e2cfa1ffc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/fb28471dd33872fbc4db6bf523f734e2cfa1ffc4"}],"sha":"67e3b887a04a34acc4c641f63285f778454d9229","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/67e3b887a04a34acc4c641f63285f778454d9229"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/fb28471dd33872fbc4db6bf523f734e2cfa1ffc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:59:45Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"sahassakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:59:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(studio): Phase 0 foundations + Page Designer canvas spike (#59)\n\n* feat(studio): feature-flag cascade service (Phase 0)\n\nPlatform → tenant → author resolution: a flag is enabled only if the platform\ndefault allows AND the tenant hasn''t disabled it AND the author hasn''t opted\nout; default OFF, no layer can force-enable past the one above. Platform\ndefaults and the tenant policy source are injectable (testable); author opt-out\npersists best-effort to localStorage. Models the aiAssistedAuthoring flag that\ngates the Phase-2 AI draft generator. Pure resolveFlag() + service covered by a\n10-case truth-table spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(studio): Angular Material 3 foundation mapped to Studio tokens (Phase 0)\n\nAdd @angular/material@21 alongside the custom design system (not replacing it).\nA new _material-theme.scss scaffolds M3 structure/density/typography (pinned to\nthe Studio''s Inter stack, not Roboto) and remaps Material''s --mat-sys-* system\ntokens onto the Studio design tokens — so Material components follow the Studio''s\nlight/dark automatically with no duplicate dark block. Wire provideAnimationsAsync\nso Material components work as they''re adopted. Adoption policy in\ndocs/material-adoption.md: Material for commodity chrome (tables, stepper,\noverlays), CDK for behaviour, custom for canvas/graph/preview. Component rollout\nis Phase 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(catalog): V3 migration for capability authoring provenance (Phase 0)\n\nAdds the authored_by column the already-merged provenance code depends on\n(Capability.authoredBy / Views / CapabilityService create+update, and the\nStudio''s ✨ AI-assisted badge). Additive, nullable, defaults to ''human'' so\nexisting rows are unaffected. Per-DB syntax for h2, postgresql (ADD COLUMN\nVARCHAR) and oracle (ADD (…) VARCHAR2).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(studio): CDK drag-drop canvas in the Page Designer (Phase 1 spike)\n\nLayer @angular/cdk/drag-drop onto the existing region model: drag a capability\nfrom the palette into a region (copy), reorder blocks within a region, and drag\nblocks across regions. All mutations go through the same regions() signal that\nserializes to the saved page body, so the drag canvas and the existing manual\npath (click-to-add + ▲▼ move buttons, keyboard-accessible) stay perfectly in\nsync — the manual path is untouched and remains the accessible fallback. Drag\nstates styled with Studio design tokens.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(studio): undo/redo for the Page Designer canvas (Phase 1)\n\nA history stack over the regions() model, recorded automatically by a signal\neffect (no per-mutation plumbing) so it covers drag-drop and every manual edit\nalike. undo/redo pre-set the tracked state so their own writes aren''t\nre-recorded; structural layout/type changes and load reset the stack. Toolbar\n↶/↷ buttons + ⌘Z / ⌘⇧Z (⌘Y) shortcuts, ignored while typing in a field. Makes\na bad canvas edit recoverable — the gap the plan flagged for JSON authoring.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(studio): CDK drag-drop + undo/redo in the Form Designer (Phase 1)\n\nReplace the Form Designer''s native HTML5 drag with @angular/cdk/drag-drop: the\ngrip is a cdkDragHandle so the row''s inputs stay interactive, palette components\ndrag into the canvas (copy), and fields reorder within it. Add structural\nundo/redo over fields() — records add/move/remove but NOT per-keystroke label\nedits (inputs keep their own native undo). Toolbar ↶/↷ + ⌘Z / ⌘⇧Z, ignored while\ntyping. Drops the native draggable/dragstart/drop handlers and the drag signal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1baff71decab457353f19406367317b802f78216","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/1baff71decab457353f19406367317b802f78216"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/fb28471dd33872fbc4db6bf523f734e2cfa1ffc4","verification":{"payload":"tree 1baff71decab457353f19406367317b802f78216\nparent f356f1a4dcc113bd738d857f4111a708762d0a40\nauthor sahassakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1787428785 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787428785 +0530\n\nfeat(studio): Phase 0 foundations + Page Designer canvas spike (#59)\n\n* feat(studio): feature-flag cascade service (Phase 0)\n\nPlatform → tenant → author resolution: a flag is enabled only if the platform\ndefault allows AND the tenant hasn''t disabled it AND the author hasn''t opted\nout; default OFF, no layer can force-enable past the one above. Platform\ndefaults and the tenant policy source are injectable (testable); author opt-out\npersists best-effort to localStorage. Models the aiAssistedAuthoring flag that\ngates the Phase-2 AI draft generator. Pure resolveFlag() + service covered by a\n10-case truth-table spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(studio): Angular Material 3 foundation mapped to Studio tokens (Phase 0)\n\nAdd @angular/material@21 alongside the custom design system (not replacing it).\nA new _material-theme.scss scaffolds M3 structure/density/typography (pinned to\nthe Studio''s Inter stack, not Roboto) and remaps Material''s --mat-sys-* system\ntokens onto the Studio design tokens — so Material components follow the Studio''s\nlight/dark automatically with no duplicate dark block. Wire provideAnimationsAsync\nso Material components work as they''re adopted. Adoption policy in\ndocs/material-adoption.md: Material for commodity chrome (tables, stepper,\noverlays), CDK for behaviour, custom for canvas/graph/preview. Component rollout\nis Phase 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(catalog): V3 migration for capability authoring provenance (Phase 0)\n\nAdds the authored_by column the already-merged provenance code depends on\n(Capability.authoredBy / Views / CapabilityService create+update, and the\nStudio''s ✨ AI-assisted badge). Additive, nullable, defaults to ''human'' so\nexisting rows are unaffected. Per-DB syntax for h2, postgresql (ADD COLUMN\nVARCHAR) and oracle (ADD (…) VARCHAR2).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(studio): CDK drag-drop canvas in the Page Designer (Phase 1 spike)\n\nLayer @angular/cdk/drag-drop onto the existing region model: drag a capability\nfrom the palette into a region (copy), reorder blocks within a region, and drag\nblocks across regions. All mutations go through the same regions() signal that\nserializes to the saved page body, so the drag canvas and the existing manual\npath (click-to-add + ▲▼ move buttons, keyboard-accessible) stay perfectly in\nsync — the manual path is untouched and remains the accessible fallback. Drag\nstates styled with Studio design tokens.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(studio): undo/redo for the Page Designer canvas (Phase 1)\n\nA history stack over the regions() model, recorded automatically by a signal\neffect (no per-mutation plumbing) so it covers drag-drop and every manual edit\nalike. undo/redo pre-set the tracked state so their own writes aren''t\nre-recorded; structural layout/type changes and load reset the stack. Toolbar\n↶/↷ buttons + ⌘Z / ⌘⇧Z (⌘Y) shortcuts, ignored while typing in a field. Makes\na bad canvas edit recoverable — the gap the plan flagged for JSON authoring.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(studio): CDK drag-drop + undo/redo in the Form Designer (Phase 1)\n\nReplace the Form Designer''s native HTML5 drag with @angular/cdk/drag-drop: the\ngrip is a cdkDragHandle so the row''s inputs stay interactive, palette components\ndrag into the canvas (copy), and fields reorder within it. Add structural\nundo/redo over fields() — records add/move/remove but NOT per-keystroke label\nedits (inputs keep their own native undo). Toolbar ↶/↷ + ⌘Z / ⌘⇧Z, ignored while\ntyping. Drops the native draggable/dragstart/drop handlers and the drag signal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqif+xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtQYQADWtdshONHwvbOfJYXScZsqG\nrI/nfdqvMX27aTe0RtK+iNSAwIGfqWvjESgl3qbn4AzUEKje7gaJ/i5P1jM0+eV5\nlSktvkc/OkF5zCnsJFnWZ3zjpdXSYC7Y0me2eXIrQm/ySUj+CPur56izAQ4j8taM\njPhwDmpNwtzyZIKdxkFySYhNjeRgsihasGnDkYhU49j5mSNurTaeZ8sbq0EXWzMa\nI43XlZB47vLCDceFxzQntd4Yr/Upo2GzC/s155YySmlIgpoMZIjJMdkUdZJY6/VR\nykZh3jnWUCE6JQgYzjiZ60GJah61fdEvOrl5LdkTwFdC3vKEj4c6pstzkZg5lsdm\nnkPLU5PoEXQY5WcDykExSIayQrb6enWd+Kp7ssnudPGES4HAAhB/UurZ0I7uL8l6\ny9bYrkZWS+9bwbSejoA/1yK7kpHZg79q/cHIDkG5t1uqTUk8hUaWug21xgJlJCrf\nUsjGT0Zf4pXgekVpqVQwztvmIo9IeyhcXvQU4l6oL1GO9sn8xUBOD84MjvlsOCVD\nqcYKj+5nEPmnHTtayApuPEj1ClBrT1p5q9wQ3oG+sJy41v7ILFs2JKUeoOzc3CQY\nZCG7z3fn8zGvyX/LAzaPRY4dITq0PI6Y0DPvDDic+HnLVb4xTGt0BWWXLZzWmJFo\nez1FLEch4UWVXGXFd9Ve