lowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/9e78a3af1f5697454451409598db716681aee8b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T11:50:01Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"sahassakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T11:50:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(publish): use npm Trusted Publishing (OIDC) instead of NPM_TOKEN (#55)\n\nnpm is deprecating the automation/granular token 2FA-bypass that direct\npublishing relied on; the token now fails with E403 ''granular access token\nwith bypass 2fa enabled is required''. Drop NODE_AUTH_TOKEN from every publish\nstep so npm (>= 11.5.1, already pinned to 11.6.2) authenticates via the\nworkflow''s OIDC token. Requires a trusted publisher configured per package on\nnpmjs.com (repo sahassakhare/agentic-ui, workflow publish.yml). id-token:write\nis already granted; provenance still works. Idempotent skip-guard unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c2fd4053d1c3b33cfeaf514df8cb8c6c905b600b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/c2fd4053d1c3b33cfeaf514df8cb8c6c905b600b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/9e78a3af1f5697454451409598db716681aee8b3","verification":{"payload":"tree c2fd4053d1c3b33cfeaf514df8cb8c6c905b600b\nparent 440b6cdb11156008f3ce62bb678b244d82976476\nauthor sahassakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1787399401 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787399401 +0530\n\nci(publish): use npm Trusted Publishing (OIDC) instead of NPM_TOKEN (#55)\n\nnpm is deprecating the automation/granular token 2FA-bypass that direct\npublishing relied on; the token now fails with E403 ''granular access token\nwith bypass 2fa enabled is required''. Drop NODE_AUTH_TOKEN from every publish\nstep so npm (>= 11.5.1, already pinned to 11.6.2) authenticates via the\nworkflow''s OIDC token. Requires a trusted publisher configured per package on\nnpmjs.com (repo sahassakhare/agentic-ui, workflow publish.yml). id-token:write\nis already granted; provenance still works. Idempotent skip-guard unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiYzpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAv4QAHvZ2c33t8M3MtCT/nwkWEab\njVDMNKlo+lVVWac3auOXsjQebADLBszlLR5x2CSEWFau80g8nFySjlFNEiGTtWgs\npC1FJHPgqqI5GYEDgwh5aKJFtTtbmNnXyUsVrmCxEs82PPkvDsJxrbldPeVe2q5G\nc5AjuURo8ZkgqrC4ukL95IvXUVCSdm41VY44bqQJu9yhd0tji9Q76udjTpS1MtDd\n4uSAXTzrS6+BeOKerUHwK8vHcZTmJZy6841J2pA+YJmInG2YRyne6pORuwZqC/1c\n7mj0zm6fzAh4NCSSxZVS6hR0foR3TcvTIQIoztha5dOCPeYksb1wGrdbNdrYz+0h\nB8lOZYsA36Acg3H33AVF6V4cQdx0SdqhLPk1RuzZWnsfg3cwLANJwyRjQY6+VW56\nvj5co4nB2aZlQO58kj1Lb9FR2HTOzgktWFpdtM0/+k9QRh8ouV9jvivCKVZzr6R0\n3CZTG7c0D22JAcTzTSYY+KF1t1PRQlwcPu0WBWj0+x1SYMs2S2dUR1Xq3IeH+90O\ndZRBpknoQyKAUl1shpiJv6L4XT9I7gVebMxwdsxWh+hcubSUSzAn7bRLtqa+g69M\n/i0ieHM4y2nF/f+UTR781pHrmlaDIMG7RaJiieyB25CYQbvU/hBA0dNE2e+h1HN+\nZfWOOfDwhXC90Seso/JX\n=NaB/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T11:50:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/9e78a3af1f5697454451409598db716681aee8b3","node_id":"C_kwDOSNG7mtoAKDllNzhhM2FmMWY1Njk3NDU0NDUxNDA5NTk4ZGI3MTY2ODFhZWU4YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/440b6cdb11156008f3ce62bb678b244d82976476","sha":"440b6cdb11156008f3ce62bb678b244d82976476","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/440b6cdb11156008f3ce62bb678b244d82976476"}],"sha":"9e78a3af1f5697454451409598db716681aee8b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/9e78a3af1f5697454451409598db716681aee8b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/440b6cdb11156008f3ce62bb678b244d82976476/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T07:21:14Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"sahassakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T07:21:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: connect-studio schematic + agentic-ui 1.5.0 release (H2 console, responsive pass) (#54)\n\n* feat(catalog): serve the H2 web console under Spring Boot 4\n\nSpring Boot 4 dropped the H2 console auto-configuration, so /h2-console 404''d\ndespite spring.h2.console.enabled: true. Register the H2 servlet explicitly\n(guarded on that property → local/dev only). H2 is runtime-scoped so the servlet\nclass isn''t on the compile classpath — instantiate it reflectively. SecurityConfig\nalready permits /h2-console/** + disables frame options.\n\nVerified: /h2-console/ → 200 (login page), alongside Swagger; catalog data intact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(studio): responsive breakpoints for three designers with fixed grids\n\napplication-designer (320px 1fr → 1col @860), requirements-builder\n(6-col dense row reflows to a two-row grid @560), capability-studio\npreview key/value pairs stack @520. Closes the last components that had\nlayout grids with no media queries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(hub): responsive breakpoints for form + dashboard widgets\n\nwidgets.ts CARD (shared by all 11 form widgets) stacks its 1fr 1fr\nfield row to a single column @480; bar-chart row tightens its fixed\nlabel/value columns @380 so the bar keeps usable width on phones.\npage-host already collapses every layout via its 900px catch-all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(schematics): connect-studio — wire an existing Angular app to the Studio catalog backend\n\nNew `ng g @infra-tools/agentic-ui:connect-studio` (alias `cs`) generalizes the\nHub''s catalog runtime bridge into a schematic any standalone app can run. It:\n\n- scaffolds a self-contained `src/app/catalog-runtime/` — a CatalogClient\n  (HTTP + one pooled SSE stream), pure compile helpers (catalog-http,\n  form-compile), and five Catalog*Source services that compile catalog rows\n  into the lib registries (experience/form/workflow/datasource/tool);\n- decouples from the Hub''s app-local AuthService/environment via CATALOG_CONFIG\n  + CATALOG_AUTH injection tokens (default disabled; OIDC via a provided token);\n- patches app.config.ts with provideCatalogRuntime({ baseUrl, tenant, … })\n  idempotently and adds the deps.\n\nThe generated bridge type-checks against the lib''s public API under full Angular\nstrictness. Snapshot-tested (2 cases) alongside the other generators.\n\nDocs: schematics cookbook (dedicated section + kind->registry table), lib README,\nroot README (13->14 generators), and the Hub README (points at the schematic as\nthe reusable form of its bridge).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(release): bump @infra-tools/agentic-ui to 1.5.0\n\nCaptures the features landed since the published 1.4.0 — design-token\nsystem, workflow decision branching, type-aware MFE remote loader — plus\nthe new connect-studio schematic. Syncs LIB_VERSION (was drifted at 1.3.0)\nand adds the 1.5.0 CHANGELOG entry.\n\nPublishes via the GitHub Actions publish workflow (workflow_dispatch or a\nGitHub Release); the idempotent job skips the other packages whose versions\nare already on npm.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(workflow-renderer): await the async step transition in F3 specs\n\nThe decision-branching feature made next() async (resolveNextAsync, so a\nDecisionNext step can run the governed evaluator). Four F3 specs still\nclicked the Next button and asserted synchronously, so the step hadn''t\ntransitioned yet — ''expected null to be truthy''. Await whenStable() after\nthe advancing click (mirrors AC-F3-1''s submit + the onComplete spec).\nback() stays synchronous. Fixes the pre-existing red on main; 10/10 pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6180a6057ab3d85747da8d915689cc103f552a36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/6180a6057ab3d85747da8d915689cc103f552a36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/440b6cdb11156008f3ce62bb678b244d82976476","verification":{"payload":"tree 6180a6057ab3d85747da8d915689cc103f552a36\nparent cf215e9be0f66e7460e1c560497cc05c546a935f\nauthor sahassakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1787210474 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787210474 +0530\n\nfeat: connect-studio schematic + agentic-ui 1.5.0 release (H2 console, responsive pass) (#54)\n\n* feat(catalog): serve the H2 web console under Spring Boot 4\n\nSpring Boot 4 dropped the H2 console auto-configuration, so /h2-console 404''d\ndespite spring.h2.console.enabled: true. Register the H2 servlet explicitly\n(guarded on that property → local/dev only). H2 is runtime-scoped so the servlet\nclass isn''t on the compile classpath — instantiate it reflectively. SecurityConfig\nalready permits /h2-console/** + disables frame options.\n\nVerified: /h2-console/ → 200 (login page), alongside Swagger; catalog data intact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(studio): responsive breakpoints for three designers with fixed grids\n\napplication-designer (320px 1fr → 1col @860), requirements-builder\n(6-col dense row reflows to a two-row grid @560), capability-studio\npreview key/value pairs stack @520. Closes the last components that had\nlayout grids with no media queries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(hub): responsive breakpoints for form + dashboard widgets\n\nwidgets.ts CARD (shared by all 11 form widgets) stacks its 1fr 1fr\nfield row to a single column @480; bar-chart row tightens its fixed\nlabel/value columns @380 so the bar keeps usable width on phones.\npage-host already collapses every layout via its 900px catch-all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(schematics): connect-studio — wire an existing Angular app to the Studio catalog backend\n\nNew `ng g @infra-tools/agentic-ui:connect-studio` (alias `cs`) generalizes the\nHub''s catalog runtime bridge into a schematic any standalone app can run. It:\n\n- scaffolds a self-contained `src/app/catalog-runtime/` — a CatalogClient\n  (HTTP + one pooled SSE stream), pure compile helpers (catalog-http,\n  form-compile), and five Catalog*Source services that compile catalog rows\n  into the lib registries (experience/form/workflow/datasource/tool);\n- decouples from the Hub''s app-local AuthService/environment via CATALOG_CONFIG\n  + CATALOG_AUTH injection tokens (default disabled; OIDC via a provided token);\n- patches app.config.ts with provideCatalogRuntime({ baseUrl, tenant, … })\n  idempotently and adds the deps.\n\nThe generated bridge type-checks against the lib''s public API under full Angular\nstrictness. Snapshot-tested (2 cases) alongside the other generators.\n\nDocs: schematics cookbook (dedicated section + kind->registry table), lib README,\nroot README (13->14 generators), and the Hub README (points at the schematic as\nthe reusable form of its bridge).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(release): bump @infra-tools/agentic-ui to 1.5.0\n\nCaptures the features landed since the published 1.4.0 — design-token\nsystem, workflow decision branching, type-aware MFE remote loader — plus\nthe new connect-studio schematic. Syncs LIB_VERSION (was drifted at 1.3.0)\nand adds the 1.5.0 CHANGELOG entry.\n\nPublishes via the GitHub Actions publish workflow (workflow_dispatch or a\nGitHub Release); the idempotent job skips the other packages whose versions\nare already on npm.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(workflow-renderer): await the async step transition in F3 specs\n\nThe decision-branching feature made next() async (resolveNextAsync, so a\nDecisionNext step can run the governed evaluator). Four F3 specs still\nclicked the Next button and asserted synchronously, so the step hadn''t\ntransitioned yet — ''expected null to be truthy''. Await whenStable() after\nthe advancing click (mirrors AC-F3-1''s submit + the onComplete spec).\nback() stays synchronous. Fixes the pre-existing red on main; 10/10 pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhqrqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArKEQAFIpl3FCL8r2N+kFOxzixzr5\n4ujc0kPr6dTBYkIIOVTpE+foacdxONpQGyH9+4USMI5fXgkkHTMP5ZzwwELSj8sI\n5Yn4GG3YM2qiR251muilpA8bGfVZQVutn3N85UljxVG9P6b14m3fDWXQ95yTNp7a\nzzOO1wgKFE30Er/R0rSfQ6yhVUSmCbEvs7xYkmgcQVvxgkJc7ge0sfFGIMvJn7tU\nORuYqTaFRbUM5f4mS0dz8F6HiMHOJv96vP3rQyClMIV7Csz/Rq07Pfw2GFheiFNs\n89H9v+nvbgByeSs0/aUQmlRrjL6RyVMu4TjOJexZUYIOaayyIyhdzhnTnG0nUu2V\nJ5nIvFvhJpG03x22dtHrvH/kJUa7Zj6/+vpGd7O0BQO12QK/Dk/y4zPIcAHiKAn9\n1e6zUGlCo5XTLQB2BGWnoH8RNHD1+rqyvduqP4BbOCZvKxkKTShJeWqItbKGJNHg\n0c+OEQjak5DgYQv1wRFuB99mZEcq9ieeLptiDeUibpmWHCAzCLeyf3sqQ4qFwPi5\n8RayA59aBcXlxCsZe+tkYEyIN15oG5hfSU7C4t4+ZOYeThp8umz3eD/GIy3jFWjl\nxLNLMAzcSDB9IhIE+