IwM2NhNzAzZmM0ZTJmMmVlODY2YjIwMDI4NGVlYWQ1MDE0MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commit/4c3ad851d836dfda19ee04736ea0e7af6a09c8fb","sha":"4c3ad851d836dfda19ee04736ea0e7af6a09c8fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/4c3ad851d836dfda19ee04736ea0e7af6a09c8fb"}],"sha":"58eb03ca703fc4e2f2ee866b200284eead501419","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/58eb03ca703fc4e2f2ee866b200284eead501419"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21344002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sahassakhare","id":21344002,"login":"sahassakhare","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQ0MDAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/4c3ad851d836dfda19ee04736ea0e7af6a09c8fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T05:12:21Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"sahassakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T05:12:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(studio): capability usage graph — what each registry item uses / is used by (#50)\n\nAuthors couldn''t tell what a capability is composed of, what depends on it, or\nwhether its references even exist — e.g. a workflow referencing components that\naren''t defined looked fine. Add a cross-registry dependency view.\n\n- kind-meta.ts: one taxonomy (glyph + label + hue) per capability kind, so a\n  page / component / experience / form / workflow / decision / tool / data source\n  are visually distinct wherever they appear.\n- CapabilityGraphService: builds the dependency graph from the IMPLICIT references\n  in each catalog body — application→pages, page→surfaces, form→components/\n  validators/data-sources/tools, workflow→components/decisions, skill→tools,\n  tool→data-source — resolves each reference to its real kind, and inverts it for\n  used-by. Flags references that resolve to nothing as UNMET.\n- Registry list rows now show \"↳ uses N · ↰ used by M · ⚠ K unmet\", expanding to\n  the specific references each labeled by kind. Unmet references are called out in\n  red — e.g. the legal-intake-matter workflow clearly shows its 6 undefined\n  component widgets instead of looking complete.\n\nStudio-only; builds clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b1ff00ce62390e5a7f4b9377f1f499a58a813542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/b1ff00ce62390e5a7f4b9377f1f499a58a813542"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/4c3ad851d836dfda19ee04736ea0e7af6a09c8fb","verification":{"payload":"tree b1ff00ce62390e5a7f4b9377f1f499a58a813542\nparent 2362857c5f1e3d94e612eaca342c65e2e984b3b3\nauthor sahassakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1787202741 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787202741 +0530\n\nfeat(studio): capability usage graph — what each registry item uses / is used by (#50)\n\nAuthors couldn''t tell what a capability is composed of, what depends on it, or\nwhether its references even exist — e.g. a workflow referencing components that\naren''t defined looked fine. Add a cross-registry dependency view.\n\n- kind-meta.ts: one taxonomy (glyph + label + hue) per capability kind, so a\n  page / component / experience / form / workflow / decision / tool / data source\n  are visually distinct wherever they appear.\n- CapabilityGraphService: builds the dependency graph from the IMPLICIT references\n  in each catalog body — application→pages, page→surfaces, form→components/\n  validators/data-sources/tools, workflow→components/decisions, skill→tools,\n  tool→data-source — resolves each reference to its real kind, and inverts it for\n  used-by. Flags references that resolve to nothing as UNMET.\n- Registry list rows now show \"↳ uses N · ↰ used by M · ⚠ K unmet\", expanding to\n  the specific references each labeled by kind. Unmet references are called out in\n  red — e.g. the legal-intake-matter workflow clearly shows its 6 undefined\n  component widgets instead of looking complete.\n\nStudio-only; builds clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhoy1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB3IQAKTix/dSq1kkNeREGyLfh4mE\nd5izH1KLWdSLtt9Z/qeT4H0DtpFExfajxiczAaLIPrPu13Oy7+CP+lt2PlsfpGqa\nhLr2XRbjrXTwLBv+/UntPWUIUFWti2L3vLTUlBTvugg/AtcTAYoleg/8ggtHxMcb\npEE/9zQdoXhnJ8om/1rZFUcjVpBEk2vCxgwIDtAiIgAYONDX6Vk/Sn+B2MuVLg2d\na+20EXJg5RGmVS46oI6i9HbbnfE4aY5DiRYr5UUu3+qCm/Vh/O+tKf6HQ9vZ28P4\n+5eA3b+od34xXv1Lm2tH5ZZnSEDbIISevI6Azbt4tQNWSJRooyi9g/ZRadMynBO0\nJ8ThJ0diLD6RIlzOrD/JKWJXgLa11ahmdVkVLTwTseXCsB2cX/7LMV2WmepTFue6\nrXrSdo9JpKKGNuwGFttaDAeNzwOVMuLbe5rxjcEMto0T85ybHHoED9Ec5h7JpNue\nCYVX8iX5Obe8ngg2OIgUnXCcUd8sTs8ANPcnyxwORR/ZNck+mPdt78tYc7wcPfzy\nnb5Rx8wu3og4/ly4raiGNaQSqbe3x/0DZ5sXVMYynDKa/kd+erk3KUgyQvVpl8Wh\n0Gk60XEPwpDKCOkv5jWWXjI2yyvYF25UfrbndNOAY6urcTqniJ44Aql1jutjpSjL\n0bL6ejIMZEw+LpN9XGnv\n=Yqcf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T05:12:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{