e/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sahassakhare","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/commits/2362857c5f1e3d94e612eaca342c65e2e984b3b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:44:13Z","email":"shapitsahas@gmail.com","name":"sahassakhare"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:44:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(demo): Angular consumer app for legal matter intake — no agentic-ui (#49)\n\nA standalone Angular application (platform/legal-intake-portal, port 4800) that\nconsumes a published experience with ONLY the zero-dep @infra-tools/aep-embed-sdk\n— not @infra-tools/agentic-ui. It''s a \"Hub without the framework\": the manifest\nships the workflow steps + the conflict-check branch; this app renders them with\nits own Angular components.\n\n- manifest.ts: the published render manifest (inlined to run offline; comment\n  shows the live createEmbedClient().getManifest() wiring).\n- intake.store.ts: a signal store that walks the workflow via the SDK''s\n  resolveNext(step.next, state), branching on conflictFound.\n- steps.ts: the portal''s own standalone step components, one per manifest widget\n  name (client / matter / conflict-check / waiver / fees / review).\n- app.ts: the wizard shell; mounts the active step via ngComponentOutlet keyed by\n  the manifest widget name.\n\nPlain @angular/build:application (esbuild), zoneless, standalone. Only platform\nimport is the embed SDK (tsconfig path added). angular.json project + README.\nBuilds clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c548cc65b9d1f345073103ec9749128082484cbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/trees/c548cc65b9d1f345073103ec9749128082484cbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sahassakhare/agentic-ui/git/commits/2362857c5f1e3d94e612eaca342c65e2e984b3b3","verification":{"payload":"tree c548cc65b9d1f345073103ec9749128082484cbc\nparent 04dd2bbaf3402b91a76c86b66e664361a7738a02\nauthor sahassakhare <shapitsahas@gmail.com> 1787168653 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787168653 +0530\n\nfeat(demo): Angular consumer app for legal matter intake — no agentic-ui (#49)\n\nA standalone Angular application (platform/legal-intake-portal, port 4800) that\nconsumes a published experience with ONLY the zero-dep @infra-tools/aep-embed-sdk\n— not @infra-tools/agentic-ui. It''s a \"Hub without the framework\": the manifest\nships the workflow steps + the conflict-check branch; this app renders them with\nits own Angular components.\n\n- manifest.ts: the published render manifest (inlined to run offline; comment\n  shows the live createEmbedClient().getManifest() wiring).\n- intake.store.ts: a signal store that walks the workflow via the SDK''s\n  resolveNext(step.next, state), branching on conflictFound.\n- steps.ts: the portal''s own standalone step components, one per manifest widget\n  name (client / matter / conflict-check / waiver / fees / review).\n- app.ts: the wizard shell; mounts the active step via ngComponentOutlet keyed by\n  the manifest widget name.\n\nPlain @angular/build:application (esbuild), zoneless, standalone. Only platform\nimport is the embed SDK (tsconfig path added). angular.json project + README.\nBuilds clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgeNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXSIQAAJ1HwK7nDKw33HPViKIMkgG\nxCUhMn8fxdvRoImXKAJX39gm3BValRQRyyQEY0ujV/PudDl3W5iynpOnvV44ywSa\nlgdperhr+xGxemEG9iypGxz3+uksSYG68Ew3reHsR1mR0ttDIi30HU38HIM0FYZy\n2w