ithub.com/jagreehal","id":3634906,"login":"jagreehal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ5MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/490a27f71a269ebafe4bb4184c2f6475b7de0045/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:29:40Z","email":"jag.reehal@gmail.com","name":"Jag Reehal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:29:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(compose): compose pages from many teams'' custom elements (#272)\n\nA model composes one page from widgets that independent teams publish as\nscript-tag custom elements. The catalog comes from each team''s build, and the\npage renders inside a host page or an MCP host.\n\n- mountly-vite-plugin: custom-elements.json carries component and prop JSDoc,\n  types as written, a JSON Schema per prop with constraints from JSDoc tags,\n  and @slot declarations. peer: true shares one framework copy across\n  distributions through the page''s import map. The build warns on callback\n  names that match native events and on slots in light-DOM builds.\n- mountly: script-tag elements project the page''s slotted children through\n  shadow DOM, including children added after mount.\n- mountly-compose (new): one catalog for the prompt, JSON Schema, validation,\n  repair, two-pass selection, edit turns and host actions, plus streaming\n  (parsePartialTree), in-place rendering and connectView for MCP Apps views.\n- mountly-mcp: mountly-mcp/compose registers a show_page tool and ui:// view,\n  so the agent composes from the catalog. The dev host answers ui/message.\n- docs/examples/ai-compose: four teams, a streaming host, an MCP server and a\n  lab that compares composition strategies and gates description changes.\n- compose-from-embeds skill for coding agents.","tree":{"sha":"c72c7c2fb088e41a6df1a7e92dc57fec40dcecbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/trees/c72c7c2fb088e41a6df1a7e92dc57fec40dcecbb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/commits/490a27f71a269ebafe4bb4184c2f6475b7de0045","verification":{"payload":"tree c72c7c2fb088e41a6df1a7e92dc57fec40dcecbb\nparent dddf65a5dd7e2aba62634af5248ec722b5c184d6\nauthor Jag Reehal <jag.reehal@gmail.com> 1790414980 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790414980 +0100\n\nfeat(compose): compose pages from many teams'' custom elements (#272)\n\nA model composes one page from widgets that independent teams publish as\nscript-tag custom elements. The catalog comes from each team''s build, and the\npage renders inside a host page or an MCP host.\n\n- mountly-vite-plugin: custom-elements.json carries component and prop JSDoc,\n  types as written, a JSON Schema per prop with constraints from JSDoc tags,\n  and @slot declarations. peer: true shares one framework copy across\n  distributions through the page''s import map. The build warns on callback\n  names that match native events and on slots in light-DOM builds.\n- mountly: script-tag elements project the page''s slotted children through\n  shadow DOM, including children added after mount.\n- mountly-compose (new): one catalog for the prompt, JSON Schema, validation,\n  repair, two-pass selection, edit turns and host actions, plus streaming\n  (parsePartialTree), in-place rendering and connectView for MCP Apps views.\n- mountly-mcp: mountly-mcp/compose registers a show_page tool and ui:// view,\n  so the agent composes from the catalog. The dev host answers ui/message.\n- docs/examples/ai-compose: four teams, a streaming host, an MCP server and a\n  lab that compares composition strategies and gates description changes.\n- compose-from-embeds skill for coding agents.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt5CECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnpUQACkAZmKEQtJSai1F9r8hBj9v\nVHax+4d8Hae8Oy50zAkCvYY+U4IT7yzkm3q2uJZI7fPrLdcejBCSlbDSlVlMH7mF\n5+vgrHX4zHPkK03W3sRLrJmcaI8mao8VyoNUhc5IhNJ0Sy0khHRJ29xqI1THSmOI\nzUUzJTguHV1ANfP2mB4YSIkLn0psntDVDp3CAGL02OEbJT/A/1HHnyq/GeECvQ/f\nWGvY0bLdk2GTQfG1hOgi3GDm82NJ2xO42xxRInKg9q9OXxYfhqYFXLOu6QeaWeWW\n81Ln+azBQsWviytnbn3cjNtodt9Yc4wMxwjsoUkrvy3hd9OX4ln9LA8kE2Pym4K0\nc7PNdhfQrwU0/keuMwb+l9amrYz0GZb2PxOss1uNNyABl5Pzg59VTLItFOsgsHzJ\nMHkIEWNfvj70sVhJR59GnTsgsag9cqdZO7RFg5KqN/ZSGMsVULCv57XwGmv34YyI\npiqTxaq1UB6p1nHrn4NSLu5gS37GBRmD7K06FYhNqKFxZQY0y20zknS/WiYWCpTH\n+Q+PCPVxmu3UHRD1PcMwhoiULBoMWkVpXHqOda8loRlfankLhTz9SX4eX8CYnIEW\nNj6dZoHczfApBaem3E9Af8S/+UZk5BXYTLZ/s42BPnMvFt/MC+YtkLU4a6VcivFi\nMgKfo6WL4K89m88iWdiE\n=+sJt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T09:29:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html