m/users/jagreehal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/24e4f9758930201de721728f9a4e561a03bd1acc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T04:05:11Z","email":"jag.reehal@gmail.com","name":"Jag Reehal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T04:05:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mountly)!: replace the island runtime with a 2.3 KB core (#244)\n\nmountly/host/auto shipped 8.2 KB gzipped across two files. The JSON\ndata-mountly-island payload, the loader registry and the twenty-odd knobs\naround them are gone; islands are plain data-* attributes and the runtime\nis one file behind mountly/auto.\n\n<mountly-feature> had its own trigger resolution, props parsing, mount-target\nhandling and lifecycle — a second implementation with a different vocabulary.\nIt now translates its attributes to the core''s and calls wire().\n\nLifecycle work for a mount target is serialized through one queue, so a\nteardown that is still unwinding can no longer erase the mount that replaced\nit, and an async update() cannot land over a newer mount. Separate triggers\npointing at the same data-target serialize with each other.\n\nSee .changeset/tiny-core.md for the full breaking list and migration.","tree":{"sha":"dba73c8034b6c7e72fedb2a1fbaa8b47c9c75ecd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/trees/dba73c8034b6c7e72fedb2a1fbaa8b47c9c75ecd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/commits/24e4f9758930201de721728f9a4e561a03bd1acc","verification":{"payload":"tree dba73c8034b6c7e72fedb2a1fbaa8b47c9c75ecd\nparent c0ca85de4b8fb38315a4da103fa89d82543e390a\nauthor Jag Reehal <jag.reehal@gmail.com> 1787544311 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787544311 +0100\n\nfeat(mountly)!: replace the island runtime with a 2.3 KB core (#244)\n\nmountly/host/auto shipped 8.2 KB gzipped across two files. The JSON\ndata-mountly-island payload, the loader registry and the twenty-odd knobs\naround them are gone; islands are plain data-* attributes and the runtime\nis one file behind mountly/auto.\n\n<mountly-feature> had its own trigger resolution, props parsing, mount-target\nhandling and lifecycle — a second implementation with a different vocabulary.\nIt now translates its attributes to the core''s and calls wire().\n\nLifecycle work for a mount target is serialized through one queue, so a\nteardown that is still unwinding can no longer erase the mount that replaced\nit, and an async update() cannot land over a newer mount. Separate triggers\npointing at the same data-target serialize with each other.\n\nSee .changeset/tiny-core.md for the full breaking list and migration.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqi8L3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqG0QAIqP9HsZFrT1Pn4m/b0vlt2D\nrL+8WlnhvxOjPvDEEHuz1zl5Fz+YvDXf9jMJg5vkCr/D9UxpkFxIz3z/zPh3nEOy\neUQKteEwIvGtG458FT5Iu/34U8e8+284zd6nCtfnEsqP6/4F0rDib8iVogsnTwpd\nYq4mxWYNTBNMsVz+zWmF/ZS8mu6GbANJ1WvbNCrX8tSNpgTQiR8sECyLsEFUFk3u\ncfxs27Wa6qVosve/2i/mG47l12yO+/D93ItWStJMJuAqqe4iO/u0K29B2J1bx6rY\nNmbZ5yuVwGl+lYqfpic4NyHUgCgELbzLXlq9D8sePMQ3xTyydlubVqn9Yvnh8BiR\nIVsPT96vw5vewUXXHw/CsckqbB52S3N3UBObF8foC02ebHzi8YPEshXNHYRJpp29\nLkcE/3wlPmRuixx5NkFt69mBYjcuKwxTBm2R56Mam3Zp1h7H/SS/2Smri+kImSWA\n0KZ3HmvXT71BFiImY9fkcV7X6WF1gtmxO+uvj5sXrPa323iwwDPc7cuAvlyCAnNg\nXQsvY3IIKTot/aaioNije3jyD2zVZvg5iFw/gHaJg4TPy1aUlxx856m3oNu4J9o8\n0HszO/wILGln7F4ceOVggFVQCGU1Yldw04+qfK+8dd7iOqKyu2sRxkiR4kfPKHSB\nKZE8pFIA2Zkew//idwiZ\n=jqCB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T04:05:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/w