s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal","id":3634906,"login":"jagreehal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ5MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/bffdef2e38a068e0ab728bc0a3f2a6bfa41cd06a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:18:12Z","email":"jag.reehal@gmail.com","name":"Jag Reehal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:18:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp)!: View-first API aligned to the Final MCP Apps spec (#229)\n\nMCP Apps went Final on 2026-01-26. The spec calls the whole server + UI\nproduct an App, and the iframe side of it a View — \"widget\" appears once\nin the entire ext-apps repo, against 458 uses of \"view\". mountly-mcp now\nspeaks that vocabulary end to end, so nothing has to be translated\nbetween the spec, the docs and the API.\n\nCore mountly stays a general-purpose UI platform and keeps its own\nWidgetModule vocabulary; mountly-mcp re-exports it as McpView so the word\nnever crosses the boundary.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: every renamed symbol is listed in the changeset. No\nback-compat aliases — mountly-mcp has no users on 3.x yet, and an alias\nper symbol is exactly the translation layer this release removes.\n\n  createMcpWidget        -> createMcpView\n  createGenerativeWidget -> createGenerativeView\n  mountlyMcpWidget       -> mountlyMcpViews\n  McpWidgetProps         -> McpViewProps\n  McpWidgetToolResult    -> McpAppToolResult\n  useMcpHost             -> useMcpApp\n  runBridge({ widget })  -> runBridge({ view })\n  __mountlyMcpWidget__   -> __mountlyMcpView__\n  widget-mount-threw     -> view-mount-threw\n\nuseMcpHost returned the ext-apps App, not the host — the same object the\nofficial SDK''s useApp() returns. Renaming it frees use*Host* to mean\nhost-side data consistently (useHostContext, useHostStyles, useHostFonts).\n\nScaffold entry is now src/view.tsx / src/view.ts, built bundles are\nview-<n>-<name>.{js,css}, and the dev host serves /view.html and\n/view.meta.json.\n\nAlso updates the four mountly-mcp skills, the MCP docs, and every example\nto the current API. docs/how-to-test.md was still showing the removed\ncreateMcpAppServer({ widgets: [...] }) shape; it now uses the one-call\nserveStdio({ views, tools }).","tree":{"sha":"cb88bfc3d688d1fdb9bdc1909497b46a98eef708","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/trees/cb88bfc3d688d1fdb9bdc1909497b46a98eef708"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/commits/bffdef2e38a068e0ab728bc0a3f2a6bfa41cd06a","verification":{"payload":"tree cb88bfc3d688d1fdb9bdc1909497b46a98eef708\nparent 38d2a047b5f2f1bcca933bc85963ee0d3293a87f\nauthor Jag Reehal <jag.reehal@gmail.com> 1787465892 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787465892 +0100\n\nfeat(mcp)!: View-first API aligned to the Final MCP Apps spec (#229)\n\nMCP Apps went Final on 2026-01-26. The spec calls the whole server + UI\nproduct an App, and the iframe side of it a View — \"widget\" appears once\nin the entire ext-apps repo, against 458 uses of \"view\". mountly-mcp now\nspeaks that vocabulary end to end, so nothing has to be translated\nbetween the spec, the docs and the API.\n\nCore mountly stays a general-purpose UI platform and keeps its own\nWidgetModule vocabulary; mountly-mcp re-exports it as McpView so the word\nnever crosses the boundary.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: every renamed symbol is listed in the changeset. No\nback-compat aliases — mountly-mcp has no users on 3.x yet, and an alias\nper symbol is exactly the translation layer this release removes.\n\n  createMcpWidget        -> createMcpView\n  createGenerativeWidget -> createGenerativeView\n  mountlyMcpWidget       -> mountlyMcpViews\n  McpWidgetProps         -> McpViewProps\n  McpWidgetToolResult    -> McpAppToolResult\n  useMcpHost             -> useMcpApp\n  runBridge({ widget })  -> runBridge({ view })\n  __mountlyMcpWidget__   -> __mountlyMcpView__\n  widget-mount-threw     -> view-mount-threw\n\nuseMcpHost returned the ext-apps App, not the host — the same object the\nofficial SDK''s useApp() returns. Renaming it frees use*Host* to mean\nhost-side data consistently (useHostContext, useHostStyles, useHostFonts).\n\nScaffold entry is now src/view.tsx / src/view.ts, built bundles are\nview-<n>-<name>.{js,css}, and the dev host serves /view.html and\n/view.meta.json.\n\nAlso updates the four mountly-mcp skills, the MCP docs, and every example\nto the current API. docs/how-to-test.md was still showing the removed\ncreateMcpAppServer({ widgets: [...] }) shape; it now uses the one-call\nserveStdio({ views, tools }).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqipCkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeywQAIcCLwk/FLUlJwtp2umLTd9m\nuck8wrIX9FG/pHw9bcAvkT6J6rX7CmNjijiFXUb4qZ0Tawx+DzsQ+VHRXY6K/bW/\nCYdEPWX6Uoxml/T2Hm91QpDmH/+j+ZHdo5xmaJQVcRsNl2fn+k1k8tMKO8Gi0vBm\nfxqpDUyFc0h6Sk+HRjEJhNIIQ7xWhr326psjlLe0uEWxg/nOsVCtCuqI+jgQ650t\neIVRjxq41MX9vEWdl6X4Od3lOdybqM/yaAfPeJWPPgMIiJHZU/t+QtkwLb6SJ2Zq\nV3o4dky2oNzRVkvn7ehciuP7s6+7FQR2IaEg46hu4JCqz0Q99jvhVqplBA7E8GpQ\nY+v4hSfHbupcv4IpldwEhw5vQNbhgNJB8M8NGN9TPHcVHqaa4IkGJvVeXH9uFMYf\nTflPrmKkA2hQrSsyn1xv7Em55HY7LDJx1zuieNRUE8cO3hfhad+8TKacGhUcMB3+\nY3fFWiRKQJJnZt/Jvp1M6l54M3FtbTNb8YUMhOqbGDLComTlUpSJQ87zVj8qaiTr\nbbbeXfE/3w9l8NjayLepEmCgN4uWUGW