}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal/mountly/commit/f19e54b4ba38b39114989500624c14738cd10352","node_id":"C_kwDOSNL879oAKGYxOWU1NGI0YmEzOGIzOTExNDk4OTUwMDYyNGMxNDczOGNkMTAzNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal/mountly/commit/a72d1b0488305d95d984c80621573e16ffc7f4b5","sha":"a72d1b0488305d95d984c80621573e16ffc7f4b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/a72d1b0488305d95d984c80621573e16ffc7f4b5"}],"sha":"f19e54b4ba38b39114989500624c14738cd10352","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/f19e54b4ba38b39114989500624c14738cd10352"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634906?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal","id":3634906,"login":"jagreehal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ5MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/a72d1b0488305d95d984c80621573e16ffc7f4b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T09:05:02Z","email":"jag.reehal@gmail.com","name":"Jag Reehal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T09:05:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mountly): iframe widgets, and fix the turbo-cache CI failure (#227)\n\n* feat(mountly): iframe widgets for verticals you cannot trust in a shared context\n\nmountly/iframe runs a widget in its own document — its own window, its own\nstyles — with the same triggers, lifecycle and custom element as a moduleUrl\nfeature. Every other distribution shares one JS context, so shadow DOM scopes\nstyles but a vertical can still mutate window and break another team at\nruntime, which quietly costs the independent deployability the split was for.\n\nmountAsFrame() in mountly/iframe/child mounts the widget the framed page\nalready ships, so one createWidget() output runs unchanged in light DOM, in a\nshadow root and in a frame: the host picks the isolation level, not the author.\n\nProps cross on a handshake rather than on load — an unmounted frame measures\nzero and a zero size is never reported, so waiting for resize-iframe''s ready\nwould deadlock the first render. The frame document is prefetched at preload\ntime, which recovers the network half of the iframe''s cost.\n\nresize-iframe is an optional peer; the child entry has no dependencies.\n\n* fix(ci): treat generated remote declarations as build outputs\n\nmountlyHostPlugin writes src/mountly-remotes.d.ts, which is gitignored and was\nnot in turbo''s build outputs. A cache hit therefore skipped the build without\nrestoring the file, and type-aware lint then failed on any host example that\nimports a remote by bare specifier — including PR #226, which changed nothing\nrelated.\n\nDeclaring them as outputs makes a cached build restore them.","tree":{"sha":"8de91827639fd20439cef8be86b2c61832852598","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/trees/8de91827639fd20439cef8be86b2c61832852598"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/commits/a72d1b0488305d95d984c80621573e16ffc7f4b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 8de91827639fd20439cef8be86b2c61832852598\nparent 1ef012b2e94e724f52277adb89e0dee8bb8be5a6\nauthor Jag Reehal <jag.reehal@gmail.com> 1787216702 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787216702 +0200\n\nfeat(mountly): iframe widgets, and fix the turbo-cache CI failure (#227)\n\n* feat(mountly): iframe widgets for verticals you cannot trust in a shared context\n\nmountly/iframe runs a widget in its own document — its own window, its own\nstyles — with the same triggers, lifecycle and custom element as a moduleUrl\nfeature. Every other distribution shares one JS context, so shadow DOM scopes\nstyles but a vertical can still mutate window and break another team at\nruntime, which quietly costs the independent deployability the split was for.\n\nmountAsFrame() in mountly/iframe/child mounts the widget the framed page\nalready ships, so one createWidget() output runs unchanged in light DOM, in a\nshadow root and in a frame: the host picks the isolation level, not the author.\n\nProps cross on a handshake rather than on load — an unmounted frame measures\nzero and a zero size is never reported, so waiting for resize-iframe''s ready\nwould deadlock the first render. The frame document is prefetched at preload\ntime, which recovers the network half of the iframe''s cost.\n\nresize-iframe is an optional peer; the child entry has no dependencies.\n\n* fix(ci): treat generated remote declarations as build outputs\n\nmountlyHostPlugin writes src/mountly-remotes.d.ts, which is gitignored and was\nnot in turbo''s build outputs. A cache hit therefore skipped the build without\nrestoring the file, and type-aware lint then failed on any host example that\nimports a remote by bare specifier — including PR #226, which changed nothing\nrelated.\n\nDeclaring them as outputs makes a cached build restore them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhsM+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAITEQAEExCKs7Y5sN6+lbHljqp7eA\nqjuEpzEfoBSGoDEmEEDb4jTwq7GTkPXK5Rd7ca0aCxbEXpo/5HkE9GCQeeciIk7B\ncCEwDzpIHE6Fyidt47pBHwzX3o8g1xXrRlY7FjH9ZM4nm/h8ibHsk2jpX6TOVZHw\nLCGlFoCKl3bA7GWSnnHS+SETtoVNtJ9JxtJbS4yZSPJTc4HnZdQ8HHsSqWpKvi5U\nmsyN1GUXQVWBax990JF998X4TyuZe/vOfDzRIsWgnaBy95kJS7u4ZxveSmUv9vt+\n7wdSu1kXz0zvheqyMmHijchhD36j9sSClLUHpw28l7/0UCh83XwNlnfhNSj6e0f0\nS5EegUWWE9FAIOsjIRvYFGzgTSAifgyUI4YJnxqlI1U/rVdIh2TPLVik8OXmto+r\n9bDY1tFPVCn9SvHEaeZLzpbOhB4fya2MKeDfJV17CulkkNrqYWy9pi35t3rotgSP\nyo0uQD5lvk3m6gb2ISXwWwwkb5+CZcYgY4c4bOHuKTQw+JM+HTRmyly2udX909Nt\nXryWI/5ZhJxdZKllif8V44OE8HrQ5jJCjyS3lmdpglveyrQlUxx39bC9wLfa7S0a\nrPLQsEcZM8pcfI5O5KFUltMN/csEj4nVMIEWC6A0ZEbDWjzBNmHagwdHgOfYiHwn\nDqAmmBDEbS5fznj8Sd02\n=dBxW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T09:05:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal/mountly/commit/a72d1b0488305d95d984c80621573e16ffc7f4b5","node_id":"C_kwDOSNL879oAKGE3MmQxYjA0ODgzMDVkOTVkOTg0YzgwNjIxNTczZTE2ZmZjN2Y0YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal/mountly/commit/1ef012b2e94e724f52277adb89e0dee8bb8be5a6","sha":"1ef012b2e94e724f52277adb89e0dee8bb8be5a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/1ef012b2e94e724f52277adb89e0dee8bb8be5a6"}],"sha":"a72d1b0488305d95d984c80621573e16ffc7f4b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/a72d1b0488305d95d984c80621573e16ffc7f4b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634906?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal","id":3634906,"login":"jagreehal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ5MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/1ef012b2e94e724f52277adb89e0dee8bb8be5a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T20:33:34Z","email":"jag.reehal@gmail.com","name":"Jag Reehal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T20:33:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp): first-class @json-render/mcp support, core 0.20, runnable example (#225)\n\n* feat(mcp): make json-render MCP support wire-compatible with @json-render/mcp\n\nThe json-render MCP facade advertised an empty tool schema\n(`{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{}}`) and a one-line description, so the\ncatalog was decorative: the model saw no component vocabulary at all.\n\n- Input schema now comes from `catalog.zodSchema()` under a `spec` argument,\n  matching @json-render/mcp. It must be a Zod raw shape — passing a bare\n  ZodType is what produced the empty schema.\n- Tool description now carries `catalog.prompt()`.\n- Tool result carries the spec in both wire formats: JSON in\n  `content[0].text` (what @json-render/mcp''s iframe hook reads) and\n  `structuredContent.spec` (what Mountly''s hosts read).\n- `useJsonRenderApp` reads either format, so an iframe built against either\n  package renders a server built with the other.\n- Input accepts the catalog schema OR a looser spec shape: core 0.19 marks\n  `visible`/`children` required on every element, which rejects most\n  first-attempt model output at the SDK gate before the handler can repair it.\n\nAlso fixes a pre-existing test race surfaced by the new test files:\nmountly-vite-plugin.story.test.ts deleted and rebuilt the committed\n`dist-exposes/` fixture that mountly-manifest.story.test.ts reads in\nparallel. It now builds into a directory it owns.\n\n* feat(mcp): bump json-render to 0.20, drop obsolete ports, add runnable example\n\nBumps @json-render/core and @json-render/react 0.19.0 -> 0.20.0 and removes\nthe two upstream fixes mountly had ported, both of which shipped in 0.20:\n\n- REQUIRED_FIELDS_RULE (#299): catalog.prompt() now carries the\n  required-`children` rule verbatim, so appending it duplicated the text.\n- pruneDanglingChildren (#300): autoFixSpec now prunes dangling child\n  references itself, with identical behaviour on all three cases mountly\n  covered — including preserving a repeat container''s dangling template\n  rather than pruning it to zero children, and the same fix message.\n\nBoth were exported from mountly-mcp/json-render/server, so this is a breaking\nexport removal; streamSpec''s behaviour is unchanged. Their unit tests are\ndropped (core owns that logic now) while the streamSpec integration test still\npins the pipeline''s pruning and prompt contract.\n\n0.20 also makes `visible` optional in the generated catalog schema, though\n`children` stays required — so the loose input branch remains, with its\ncomment updated to the narrower reason.\n\nAdds docs/examples/json-render-mcp as a runnable workspace example: one\ncatalog drives the MCP tool schema, the tool description and the React\ncomponents in the iframe, with verify.mjs asserting the whole flow in-process\nand serve-stdio.mjs for a real host.\n\n* fix(tests): stop CJS import poisoning, format repo, harden build-driven tests\n\ntests/json-render-app-e2e.spec.ts statically imported package source. Playwright\ntranspiles specs to CJS, so that pulled src/html.ts into the CJS registry and the\nfive later specs that `import()` the same source as ESM failed with \"does not\nprovide an export named ''escapeInlineScript''\". It now imports dynamically, the\nconvention tests/mcp-dev-host.story.spec.ts already documents.\n\nAlso, all pre-existing formatting drift is resolved (line wrapping only, no\nsemantic change), and three sources of load-dependent flakiness are fixed:\n\n- Tests running real Vite/esbuild builds had no explicit timeout, so they raced\n  vitest''s 5s default and failed on a cold cache. mountly-vite-plugin,\n  mcp-vite and mcp-demo now allow 30s.\n- npm-consumer''s renderedText threw when Vite''s post-optimize reload destroyed\n  the execution context mid-evaluate, aborting the surrounding poll. A\n  transient reload now reads as \"nothing rendered yet\" and the poll retries;\n  a page that never renders still fails on the poll''s own timeout.\n- npm-consumer''s run() swallowed stdout/stderr, so any failure surfaced as a\n  bare \"Command failed\". It now includes the piped output.\n\nVerified: unit suite green three consecutive runs (147 tests), full Playwright\nsuite exits 0 under the CI retry policy (219 passed, 2 flaky in unrelated\nnetwork/server-timing specs), lint, format, typecheck and all four MCP example\nverifications pass.","tree":{"sha":"24269cb3edd029202e785c853040b17c7770ecef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/trees/24269cb3edd029202e785c853040b17c7770ecef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/commits/1ef012b2e94e724f52277adb89e0dee8bb8be5a6","verification":{"payload":"tree 24269cb3edd029202e785c853040b17c7770ecef\nparent a0d2a0f5727590292c96efea37547a4f0ac3f25f\nauthor Jag Reehal <jag.reehal@gmail.com> 1787171614 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787171614 +0200\n\nfeat(mcp): first-class @json-render/mcp support, core 0.20, runnable example (#225)\n\n* feat(mcp): make json-render MCP support wire-compatible with @json-render/mcp\n\nThe json-render MCP facade advertised an empty tool schema\n(`{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{}}`) and a one-line description, so the\ncatalog was decorative: the model saw no component vocabulary at all.\n\n- Input schema now comes from `catalog.zodSchema()` under a `spec` argument,\n  matching @json-render/mcp. It must be a Zod raw shape — passing a bare\n  ZodType is what produced the empty schema.\n- Tool description now carries `catalog.prompt()`.\n- Tool result carries the spec in both wire formats: JSON in\n  `content[0].text` (what @json-render/mcp''s iframe hook reads) and\n  `structuredContent.spec` (what Mountly''s hosts read).\n- `useJsonRenderApp` reads either format, so an iframe built against either\n  package renders a server built with the other.\n- Input accepts the catalog schema OR a looser spec shape: core 0.19 marks\n  `visible`/`children` required on every element, which rejects most\n  first-attempt model output at the SDK gate before the handler can repair it.\n\nAlso fixes a pre-existing test race surfaced by the new test files:\nmountly-vite-plugin.story.test.ts deleted and rebuilt the committed\n`dist-exposes/` fixture that mountly-manifest.story.test.ts reads in\nparallel. It now builds into a directory it owns.\n\n* feat(mcp): bump json-render to 0.20, drop obsolete ports, add runnable example\n\nBumps @json-render/core and @json-render/react 0.19.0 -> 0.20.0 and removes\nthe two upstream fixes mountly had ported, both of which shipped in 0.20:\n\n- REQUIRED_FIELDS_RULE (#299): catalog.prompt() now carries the\n  required-`children` rule verbatim, so appending it duplicated the text.\n- pruneDanglingChildren (#300): autoFixSpec now prunes dangling child\n  references itself, with identical behaviour on all three cases mountly\n  covered — including preserving a repeat container''s dangling template\n  rather than pruning it to zero children, and the same fix message.\n\nBoth were exported from mountly-mcp/json-render/server, so this is a breaking\nexport removal; streamSpec''s behaviour is unchanged. Their unit tests are\ndropped (core owns that logic now) while the streamSpec integration test still\npins the pipeline''s pruning and prompt contract.\n\n0.20 also makes `visible` optional in the generated catalog schema, though\n`children` stays required — so the loose input branch remains, with its\ncomment updated to the narrower reason.\n\nAdds docs/examples/json-render-mcp as a runnable workspace example: one\ncatalog drives the MCP tool schema, the tool description and the React\ncomponents in the iframe, with verify.mjs asserting the whole flow in-process\nand serve-stdio.mjs for a real host.\n\n* fix(tests): stop CJS import poisoning, format repo, harden build-driven tests\n\ntests/json-render-app-e2e.spec.ts statically imported package source. Playwright\ntranspiles specs to CJS, so that pulled src/html.ts into the CJS registry and the\nfive later specs that `import()` the same source as ESM failed with \"does not\nprovide an export named ''escapeInlineScript''\". It now imports dynamically, the\nconvention tests/mcp-dev-host.story.spec.ts already documents.\n\nAlso, all pre-existing formatting drift is resolved (line wrapping only, no\nsemantic change), and three sources of load-dependent flakiness are fixed:\n\n- Tests running real Vite/esbuild builds had no explicit timeout, so they raced\n  vitest''s 5s default and failed on a cold cache. mountly-vite-plugin,\n  mcp-vite and mcp-demo now allow 30s.\n- npm-consumer''s renderedText threw when Vite''s post-optimize reload destroyed\n  the execution context mid-evaluate, aborting the surrounding poll. A\n  transient reload now reads as \"nothing rendered yet\" and the poll retries;\n  a page that never renders still fails on the poll''s own timeout.\n- npm-consumer''s run() swallowed stdout/stderr, so any failure surfaced as a\n  bare \"Command failed\". It now includes the piped output.\n\nVerified: unit suite green three consecutive runs (147 tests), full Playwright\nsuite exits 0 under the CI retry policy (219 passed, 2 flaky in unrelated\nnetwork/server-timing specs), lint, format, typecheck and all four MCP example\nverifications pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhhMeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMVIQAEIsDSbLGc40qkYPWJYtL9Xk\n9rLjidKuKHemslSKsWNam0r4oUTFCc7KrKbFcOwY6wtsaZuxOxXLXmYeIWY81IdD\nRUR05MMjvR50Xi5I3EYcy3KyLCaDVG83kIGZM3sjdv2N1nxjf69s/WyIGpv822y/\n7bpWvJ19giPPBda+wPsMYDGOdJAQv2edmoC9n/6ns3UAbBywr1df4L3tqHL/USf6\nA3ZncSA1mV9+DSyXAulMpqsrDwuPZznz+Fy94cUm5+EHscZIt7MPdp103i+5RgWK\n