2ad7d913b7feaf6d8134c37e89b8ab7731f9b51c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634906?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal","id":3634906,"login":"jagreehal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ5MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/59b8c0a42504742635f780a09a6bd3c68ad3e52e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T20:59:58Z","email":"jag.reehal@gmail.com","name":"Jag Reehal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T20:59:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: render Mermaid diagrams, and put MCP Apps on the landing page (#222)\n\nStarlight sends every fenced block to Expressive Code, so the decision ladder\non \"Choosing an architecture\" rendered as syntax-highlighted source rather than\na diagram. A small `<Mermaid>` component renders it in the browser: Astro ships\nthe script only on pages that import it, so the rest of the site is unaffected,\nand the build needs no headless browser. The diagram carries an aria-label\ndescribing the ladder in prose, and falls back to the source if it fails.\n\nThe landing page never mentioned MCP Apps, which is half of what mountly now\ndoes. Adds it to the hero, a use-case cell, and the package list.","tree":{"sha":"26c5a4b96bf7179bf08f2e494443a4c1b6757304","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/trees/26c5a4b96bf7179bf08f2e494443a4c1b6757304"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/commits/59b8c0a42504742635f780a09a6bd3c68ad3e52e","verification":{"payload":"tree 26c5a4b96bf7179bf08f2e494443a4c1b6757304\nparent 4e2da680d61a254c2691fc9fb0d1f9a50e71646a\nauthor Jag Reehal <jag.reehal@gmail.com> 1787000398 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787000398 +0200\n\ndocs: render Mermaid diagrams, and put MCP Apps on the landing page (#222)\n\nStarlight sends every fenced block to Expressive Code, so the decision ladder\non \"Choosing an architecture\" rendered as syntax-highlighted source rather than\na diagram. A small `<Mermaid>` component renders it in the browser: Astro ships\nthe script only on pages that import it, so the rest of the site is unaffected,\nand the build needs no headless browser. The diagram carries an aria-label\ndescribing the ladder in prose, and falls back to the source if it fails.\n\nThe landing page never mentioned MCP Apps, which is half of what mountly now\ndoes. Adds it to the hero, a use-case cell, and the package list.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg3ZOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuN0QAJV6/m+ivmDZTHAx8b6xNz7K\n4X5UpFTqsbCLWsw07C/rbn9bOkn1D9+JpV2aTqetDuNQxK2cveKHpzyBfk4ngM5B\noQlkJge5nD8gA403k3SOyxJu7a4ugNVoFJwLJ6otNeYezGSVsLCRXYFdI8lg19HL\n0/9T3fJBmJERzKatUugVjuXRhCtwgl/cd2Q4dOViplSQgtyTDhyW/a22fTSaI3hP\n+9t7e14NXjrERe2rZcgJ7yetW5+TegXirNxK5SVhvV9bCi2qUyHYzS6oxM1IaCO2\n42052b6n0iybmwsNttdO+HkLb6SoPdOWWOtkKuQ6ZwM1si2b5LRZ0c58FGD2drdV\niS+aUhBdspFD8CMG8bksxlxmqGA537/Ri0OgS6SLspto/9Qv5f6BsN4z2nqgbNJI\npk5swp+CsrNOgRKXhuX7JFuvkVR1iT4hAcBlfhJii9JGdYkfsw5YterELxFSxFfc\nomUFDn1oBzhLHvYJyn+YnI6HtRW67UXr9vDVelUik6xvgk1GSoU+KMWi49kfKB5H\nlr6UnT6abSx1MTGxbWrDAd/OmmzRKtlpfgJjbKvbaIGXbo5QSvIrZdW2ic/NyQmq\nI0D7gYyDAFm3cbG3Jf0fKK+NWB