MyNjkxZmM5ZmIwZDFmOWE1MGU3MTY0NmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal/mountly/commit/c07ea659f958373d473b74822c610c72441da351","sha":"c07ea659f958373d473b74822c610c72441da351","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/c07ea659f958373d473b74822c610c72441da351"}],"sha":"4e2da680d61a254c2691fc9fb0d1f9a50e71646a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/4e2da680d61a254c2691fc9fb0d1f9a50e71646a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634906?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal","id":3634906,"login":"jagreehal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ5MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/c07ea659f958373d473b74822c610c72441da351/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T18:24:12Z","email":"jag.reehal@gmail.com","name":"Jag Reehal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T18:24:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp)!: audit assembled Views for accessibility, and unify the registration vocabulary (#220)\n\n* feat(mcp)!: audit assembled Views for accessibility, and unify the registration vocabulary\n\n`verify --render` now runs axe against a View that mounted, reporting each\nviolation as a `render/a11y` warning. Components can each be accessible while\nthe View composing them is not — a missing label or a heading order only exists\nonce the parts are together — and the composition is what a host renders.\nWarnings, so only `--strict` fails on them. axe-core joins Playwright as an\noptional peer, evaluated through the debugger protocol so it reaches the View\nwithout the CSP granting `unsafe-eval`.\n\n`createMcpAppServer()` takes the same `views` and `tools` as `registerMcpApps()`.\nIt was already a thin façade over it, but accepted a second vocabulary that\nneeded dedup logic because the old shape repeated a View once per tool.\n\n`typescript` becomes an optional peer of `mountly-vite-plugin` rather than a\nhard dependency: it powers the fragment''s `types` block and declaration emit and\nnothing else, and a build without it still produces a fragment.\n\nAlso adds the missing READMEs for `mountly-manifest` and `mountly-vite-plugin`,\nand records why `mcp-release-readiness` typechecks with `tsc` rather than\n`vue-tsc`.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `createMcpAppServer({ widgets: [{ uri, htmlPath, tool }] })` is\nnow `createMcpAppServer({ views: [{ uri, artifact }], tools: [...] })`. The\n`McpWidgetRegistration` and `McpWidgetTool` types are removed.\n\n* build: stop formatting changeset-generated CHANGELOGs\n\n`changeset version` writes them in its own style on every release, so the\nrelease PR merged as #219 left `format:check` failing on main.","tree":{"sha":"1af523079a25634e04a9c4833144c5381f7c3312","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/trees/1af523079a25634e04a9c4833144c5381f7c3312"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/commits/c07ea659f958373d473b74822c610c72441da351","verification":{"payload":"tree 1af523079a25634e04a9c4833144c5381f7c3312\nparent a28338245fd2ed96daf2c6bb78a541041be52574\nauthor Jag Reehal <jag.reehal@gmail.com> 1786991052 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786991052 +0200\n\nfeat(mcp)!: audit assembled Views for accessibility, and unify the registration vocabulary (#220)\n\n* feat(mcp)!: audit assembled Views for accessibility, and unify the registration vocabulary\n\n`verify --render` now runs axe against a View that mounted, reporting each\nviolation as a `render/a11y` warning. Components can each be accessible while\nthe View composing them is not — a missing label or a heading order only exists\nonce the parts are together — and the composition is what a host renders.\nWarnings, so only `--strict` fails on them. axe-core joins Playwright as an\noptional peer, evaluated through the debugger protocol so it reaches the View\nwithout the CSP granting `unsafe-eval`.\n\n`createMcpAppServer()` takes the same `views` and `tools` as `registerMcpApps()`.\nIt was already a thin façade over it, but accepted a second vocabulary that\nneeded dedup logic because the old shape repeated a View once per tool.\n\n`typescript` becomes an optional peer of `mountly-vite-plugin` rather than a\nhard dependency: it powers the fragment''s `types` block and declaration emit and\nnothing else, and a build without it still produces a fragment.\n\nAlso adds the missing READMEs for `mountly-manifest` and `mountly-vite-plugin`,\nand records why `mcp-release-readiness` typechecks with `tsc` rather than\n`vue-tsc`.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `createMcpAppServer({ widgets: [{ uri, htmlPath, tool }] })` is\nnow `createMcpAppServer({ views: [{ uri, artifact }], tools: [...] })`. The\n`McpWidgetRegistration` and `McpWidgetTool` types are removed.\n\n* build: stop formatting changeset-generated CHANGELOGs\n\n`changeset version` writes them in its own style on every release, so the\nrelease PR merged as #219 left `format:check` failing on main.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg1HMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI0AQAGpsEjy2lJYpc5ouGLBcG+qK\nnMIwYV6KHs/TziGsibJXKaFMbUpPDySHC9sLRHvE6DywUzbEgfg4UDuJ9W8pWMio\nx3qrjMV8pKtaLXciS