received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal/mountly/commit/a28338245fd2ed96daf2c6bb78a541041be52574","node_id":"C_kwDOSNL879oAKGEyODMzODI0NWZkMmVkOTZkYWYyYzZiYjc4YTU0MTA0MWJlNTI1NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal/mountly/commit/5c5f0220adc3c44c0c74b18782cac498fa773b1d","sha":"5c5f0220adc3c44c0c74b18782cac498fa773b1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/5c5f0220adc3c44c0c74b18782cac498fa773b1d"}],"sha":"a28338245fd2ed96daf2c6bb78a541041be52574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/a28338245fd2ed96daf2c6bb78a541041be52574"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634906?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal","id":3634906,"login":"jagreehal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ5MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/5c5f0220adc3c44c0c74b18782cac498fa773b1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T10:45:16Z","email":"jag.reehal@gmail.com","name":"Jag Reehal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T10:45:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp)!: MCP Apps development host, verification, and a TypeScript 7 build (#218)\n\nTurn existing React, Vue and Svelte components into versioned MCP Apps Views\nthat install into the server the application already owns.\n\n- `mountly-mcp dev` serves a View in a real two-origin host with the official\n  AppBridge, a sandbox proxy enforcing the sidecar''s CSP, and `--server` for\n  driving real tool handlers in-process.\n- `mountly-mcp build` emits an App manifest; `mountlyMcpWidget({ apps })` builds\n  many independent Views from one Vite config.\n- `registerMcpApps()` installs Views and linked tools into an unconnected\n  `McpServer`, leaving transport, auth and deployment under application control.\n- `mountly-mcp verify [--render]` is one conformance engine for local use and\n  CI, loading each View in a browser and failing on timeouts, mount errors and\n  empty roots.\n\nDeclarations now come from `tsc --emitDeclarationOnly` rather than tsup''s dts\nstep, and `mountlyManifestFragmentPlugin` reads exports from the TypeScript\nchecker: TypeScript 7 is the native compiler and no longer ships the classic\nin-process compiler API.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `mountly-mcp` re-exports the MCP Apps spec type names from\n`@modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps` instead of its own aliases — `DisplayMode` is\n`McpUiDisplayMode`, `McpHost` is `App`, and so on. The changeset lists every\nrename.","tree":{"sha":"6e634d5aed0d2775b2d6fe41608cbac09152b600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/trees/6e634d5aed0d2775b2d6fe41608cbac09152b600"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/commits/5c5f0220adc3c44c0c74b18782cac498fa773b1d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e634d5aed0d2775b2d6fe41608cbac09152b600\nparent 311434228f91b55b4d67680d5bcaa4c99e3d1647\nauthor Jag Reehal <jag.reehal@gmail.com> 1786963516 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786963516 +0200\n\nfeat(mcp)!: MCP Apps development host, verification, and a TypeScript 7 build (#218)\n\nTurn existing React, Vue and Svelte components into versioned MCP Apps Views\nthat install into the server the application already owns.\n\n- `mountly-mcp dev` serves a View in a real two-origin host with the official\n  AppBridge, a sandbox proxy enforcing the sidecar''s CSP, and `--server` for\n  driving real tool handlers in-process.\n- `mountly-mcp build` emits an App manifest; `mountlyMcpWidget({ apps })` builds\n  many independent Views from one Vite config.\n- `registerMcpApps()` installs Views and linked tools into an unconnected\n  `McpServer`, leaving transport, auth and deployment under application control.\n- `mountly-mcp verify [--render]` is one conformance engine for local use and\n  CI, loading each View in a browser and failing on timeouts, mount errors and\n  empty roots.\n\nDeclarations now come from `tsc --emitDeclarationOnly` rather than tsup''s dts\nstep, and `mountlyManifestFragmentPlugin` reads exports from the TypeScript\nchecker: TypeScript 7 is the native compiler and no longer ships the classic\nin-process compiler API.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `mountly-mcp` re-exports the MCP Apps spec type names from\n`@modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps` instead of its own aliases — `DisplayMode` is\n`McpUiDisplayMode`, `McpHost` is `App`, and so on. The changeset lists every\nrename.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqguY8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ3AQAIO9dyX6RVY4Iji4AN/VJSC1\nyYGhbzpkL0Q1iHL9r1wDdfW9+mF1s3UL70Pb+B9FJEcOPWYyVkYsbMXSO2RAx3PE\nBYLDoyOtW4VMLapZjL/lsvNetJiakfVeybSHzeX8SJI6SbbAN0qRgzf9ist11xZb\nM79vGoTUuKShjx8fO9SvPz+q2M3YTPMiwZskxw1vfTRT+cwiFtlbmnV8lpa/8XpJ\nGCmqzv6ZyHJcnLjzyf5JwMyetxkbWLm1q4m1UsXltoW2wS7nltzCYIVhyBzDRQe/\nEMG1hV6G/K