ons_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal/mountly/commit/bc909a235de7e59a6935f5d45b56d1c6807cc99d","node_id":"C_kwDOSNL879oAKGJjOTA5YTIzNWRlN2U1OWE2OTM1ZjVkNDViNTZkMWM2ODA3Y2M5OWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal/mountly/commit/9865d9273390aa0894c8bb58f0d8bd293043daf1","sha":"9865d9273390aa0894c8bb58f0d8bd293043daf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/9865d9273390aa0894c8bb58f0d8bd293043daf1"}],"sha":"bc909a235de7e59a6935f5d45b56d1c6807cc99d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/bc909a235de7e59a6935f5d45b56d1c6807cc99d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3634906?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jagreehal","id":3634906,"login":"jagreehal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQ5MDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jagreehal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/commits/9865d9273390aa0894c8bb58f0d8bd293043daf1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T22:17:23Z","email":"jag.reehal@gmail.com","name":"Jag Reehal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T22:17:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(docs): repair every hosted example, restore the docs deploy (#180)\n\n* fix(docs): repair every hosted example, restore the docs deploy\n\nThe Pages deploy has been failing since #179 and every live example link\nwas 404ing before that. Four separate causes.\n\n1. Docs deploy. deploy-docs.yml runs `pnpm --filter mountly-docs build`\n   directly, so stage-examples has to build the packages it stages —\n   nothing else will. #179 removed that call to stop it racing turbo.\n   Restored, with the race handled where it belongs: the root `build`\n   script already runs turbo in two passes, docs last and alone, so the\n   nested build never runs concurrently with turbo''s.\n\n2. Every example link 404''d. `EXAMPLES_BASE` concatenated\n   `import.meta.env.BASE_URL` with \"examples/\", and BASE_URL is\n   \"/mountly\" without a trailing slash — so every link and iframe on\n   /examples/ pointed at /mountlyexamples/. Normalise the slash.\n\n3. vite-host-import loaded no remotes. mountlyHostPlugin injected the\n   import map without applying Vite''s `base`. Import maps resolve\n   against the document, so a host under a sub-path emitted\n   /remote/dist/Badge.js and hit the origin root. Now base-prefixed for\n   production builds; absolute, protocol-relative and data: URLs pass\n   through, and a \"/\" base is a no-op. Patch changeset + unit test.\n\n4. vite-host-remotes-url pointed at a dead port. It is built against a\n   throwaway local server, which baked http://127.0.0.1:5291 into its\n   import map. The same remote dist is already staged under\n   vite-host-import, so the staging pass repoints it there.\n\nThe MCP app preview is delisted as local-only rather than fixed: MCP\nApps §8.4 requires host and sandbox on different origins and Pages\nserves one. Its `verify` script still runs it locally on two ports.\n\nVerified against the built site over HTTP with a real browser: all 14\nhostable examples load with no console errors and no failed requests.\n\n* test: cover the examples as deployed, under the /mountly base\n\nFour base-path bugs shipped together and none were visible to the suite,\nbecause every webServer in playwright.config.ts runs a dev server at the\norigin root where BASE_URL is \"/\". The deployed shape was untested.\n\nAdds a static server for docs/dist under /mountly and one spec that\nreads the live examples index, asserts every link keeps the base, then\nloads each one checking status, console errors, failed requests and\nrendered content.\n\nThe list is derived from the built page rather than hardcoded, so a link\nadded to the index is covered without touching the spec.\n\nVerified it fails on the bug it guards: restoring the BASE_URL\nconcatenation turns it red, the fix turns it green.\n\n* ci: let the changeset guard pass on release PRs\n\n`changeset status` fails whenever packages changed without a changeset,\nwhich is every release PR by definition — it consumes changesets and\nadds none. #178 merged with this check red because it cannot go green.\n\nSkip the guard when the diff deletes .changeset/*.md, which is what a\nrelease PR looks like and nothing else does. No workflow expressions,\nso no untrusted input reaches the shell.\n\nVerified against both shapes: #178''s branch deletes two changesets and\nskips; this branch deletes none and runs the check as before.","tree":{"sha":"218c132de4c1aa4ecb0b92403661c9c55e7c0fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/trees/218c132de4c1aa4ecb0b92403661c9c55e7c0fc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jagreehal/mountly/git/commits/9865d9273390aa0894c8bb58f0d8bd293043daf1","verification":{"payload":"tree 218c132de4c1aa4ecb0b92403661c9c55e7c0fc3\nparent 971f19366408360c79c60c51c58104a13d031998\nauthor Jag Reehal <jag.reehal@gmail.com> 1785104243 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785104243 +0100\n\nfix(docs): repair every hosted example, restore the docs deploy (#180)\n\n* fix(docs): repair every hosted example, restore the docs deploy\n\nThe Pages deploy has been failing since #179 and every live example link\nwas 404ing before that. Four separate causes.\n\n1. Docs deploy. deploy-docs.yml runs `pnpm --filter mountly-docs build`\n   directly, so stage-examples has to build the packages it stages —\n   nothing else will. #179 removed that call to stop it racing turbo.\n   Restored, with the race handled where it belongs: the root `build`\n   script already runs turbo in two passes, docs last and alone, so the\n   nested build never runs concurrently with turbo''s.\n\n2. Every example link 404''d. `EXAMPLES_BASE` concatenated\n   `import.meta.env.BASE_URL` with \"examples/\", and BASE_URL is\n   \"/mountly\" without a trailing slash — so every link and iframe on\n   /examples/ pointed at /mountlyexamples/. Normalise the slash.\n\n3. vite-host-import loaded no remotes. mountlyHostPlugin injected the\n   import map without applying Vite''s `base`. Import maps resolve\n   against the document, so a host under a sub-path emitted\n   /remote/dist/Badge.js and hit the origin root. Now base-prefixed for\n   production builds; absolute, protocol-relative and data: URLs pass\n   through, and a \"/\" base is a no-op. Patch changeset + unit test.\n\n4. vite-host-remotes-url pointed at a dead port. It is built against a\n   throwaway local server, which baked http://127.0.0.1:5291 into its\n   import map. The same remote dist is already staged under\n   vite-host-import, so the staging pass repoints it there.\n\nThe MCP app preview is delisted as local-only rather than fixed: MCP\nApps §8.4 requires host and sandbox on different origins and Pages\nserves one. Its `verify` script still runs it locally on two ports.\n\nVerified against the built site over HTTP with a real browser: all 14\nhostable examples load with no console errors and no failed requests.\n\n* test: cover the examples as deployed, under the /mountly base\n\nFour base-path bugs shipped together and none were visible to the suite,\nbecause every webServer in playwright.config.ts runs a dev server at the\norigin root where BASE_URL is \"/\". The deployed shape was untested.\n\nAdds a static server for docs/dist under /mountly and one spec that\nreads the live examples index, asserts every link keeps the base, then\nloads each one checking status, console errors, failed requests and\nrendered content.\n\nThe list is derived from the built page rather than hardcoded, so a link\nadded to the index is covered without touching the spec.\n\nVerified it fails on the bug it guards: restoring the BASE_URL\nconcatenation turns it red, the fix turns it green.\n\n* ci: let the changeset guard pass on release PRs\n\n`changeset status` fails whenever packages changed without a changeset,\nwhich is every release PR by definition — it consumes changesets and\nadds none. #178 merged with this check red because it cannot go green.\n\nSkip the guard when the diff deletes .changeset/*.md, which is what a\nrelease PR looks like and nothing else does. No workflow expressions,\nso no untrusted input reaches the shell.\n\nVerified against both shapes: #178''s branch deletes two changesets and\nskips; this branch deletes none and runs the check as before.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZodzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPHsQAA5mP1v+F2Rq+5Gi3qRhc3x9\niHvgcYrjQLOD1KmbGa8c/nhli9gTnEVKGlH/0PeZb9xGQU49k3lmqe2wZawyV+lo\n8Zb8U1ZPXNfC1foRbiT2Eq7qtUbVT2MPVGVORJnf/HZJenEDX3hcydVJz1CubFwQ\nlux19UYgrriV9sy9chdBlm8N+RvFgQ7IdMu5daiFH8O6/wXU3N1Fm9GhhG8fhsCa\nlnLbagUOAOCSofh+inK/y31QKVA8IykmDGWYlbGNfYDlswijxM+8KTqd2H3Cxbog\n/GVhK+fro1+ezNL0lH51JFOqMHAKxjMCJjiHuY7j7bzWsCV1EZsYM