mail.com","name":"Aleksandr Cherkas"},"message":"Add fleet lifecycle, swarms & registries to orchestration\n\nCloses the fleet-lifecycle gap (and the registry/discovery question):\noperating many agents over time, distinct from building one orchestration.\nAdds four primary-source pages — the swarm-topology survey (flat/\nhierarchical/team/society/hybrid + turn-taking + static-vs-dynamic),\nSWARM+ (O(n^2) -> hierarchical-tree scaling + resilience), Kubernetes\nAgent Sandbox (warm pools, scale-to-zero-with-resume, stable identity),\nand the AWS AgentCore Agent Registry (governed publish/review/approve\ndiscovery, Preview) — plus a \"Fleet lifecycle, swarms & registries\"\nTools subsection and a \"Scaling to a fleet\" note in the reference\narchitecture. Discovery framed three ways (platform registry / A2A Agent\nCards / infra identity). Reuses the existing MAST page for the reliability\ncounterweight: coordination, not agent count, is the binding constraint\n(SOTA swarms fail 41-86.7%). From a June 2026 deep-research pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b25b8fbf287a12eda72234c740a8f82cd1851c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/git/trees/7b25b8fbf287a12eda72234c740a8f82cd1851c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/git/commits/e546ddbe6d8998d24013da3855f23cb205975ff0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7316197?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alcherkas","id":7316197,"login":"alcherkas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTYxOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/alcherkas/claude/commit/e546ddbe6d8998d24013da3855f23cb205975ff0","node_id":"C_kwDOSNOf29oAKGU1NDZkZGJlNmQ4OTk4ZDI0MDEzZGEzODU1ZjIzY2IyMDU5NzVmZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alcherkas/claude/commit/9868fdc02a1cdca78cf893e14c435c6a824b9d57","sha":"9868fdc02a1cdca78cf893e14c435c6a824b9d57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/commits/9868fdc02a1cdca78cf893e14c435c6a824b9d57"}],"sha":"e546ddbe6d8998d24013da3855f23cb205975ff0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/commits/e546ddbe6d8998d24013da3855f23cb205975ff0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7316197?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alcherkas","id":7316197,"login":"alcherkas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTYxOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/commits/9868fdc02a1cdca78cf893e14c435c6a824b9d57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-28T19:39:34Z","email":"cherkasalexandr@gmail.com","name":"Aleksandr Cherkas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T19:39:34Z","email":"cherkasalexandr@gmail.com","name":"Aleksandr Cherkas"},"message":"Add model gateway & cost routing (LiteLLM/OpenRouter/Portkey) to orchestration\n\nCloses the model-gateway gap: the control plane an orchestration calls\nthrough to reach providers — one OpenAI-compatible interface plus\nrouting, fallbacks, and caching, and the direct lever on the topic''s\n~4-15x token-cost concern. Adds three primary-source pages framing the\nself-host (LiteLLM, MIT, zero markup) vs hosted-percentage (OpenRouter,\n5.5% credit fee) vs managed-by-logs (Portkey, semantic caching) tradeoff,\nplus a \"Model gateway & cost routing\" Tools subsection and a cost-control\nnote in the reference architecture (with the ~$3,600/mo LiteLLM/OpenRouter\nbreak-even). From a June 2026 deep-research pass — 8 findings verified\nunanimous 3-0 against primary vendor docs; over-precise latency/exclusivity\nclaims refuted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"38ebbf16a1a6bb79b50ebe4d90ef92be6ace204a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/git/trees/38ebbf16a1a6bb79b50ebe4d90ef92be6ace204a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/git/commits/9868fdc02a1cdca78cf893e14c435c6a824b9d57","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7316197?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alcherkas","id":7316197,"login":"alcherkas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTYxOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/alcherkas/claude/commit/9868fdc02a1cdca78cf893e14c435c6a824b9d57","node_id":"C_kwDOSNOf29oAKDk4NjhmZGMwMmExY2RjYTc4Y2Y4OTNlMTRjNDM1YzZhODI0YjlkNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alcherkas/claude/commit/425de47731495b531a661abd27b85cce498f190b","sha":"425de47731495b531a661abd27b85cce498f190b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/commits/425de47731495b531a661abd27b85cce498f190b"}],"sha":"9868fdc02a1cdca78cf893e14c435c6a824b9d57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/commits/9868fdc02a1cdca78cf893e14c435c6a824b9d57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7316197?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alcherkas","id":7316197,"login":"alcherkas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTYxOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alcherkas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/commits/425de47731495b531a661abd27b85cce498f190b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-28T19:24:30Z","email":"cherkasalexandr@gmail.com","name":"Aleksandr Cherkas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T19:24:30Z","email":"cherkasalexandr@gmail.com","name":"Aleksandr Cherkas"},"message":"Add SAST/SCA & incident-response sources + worked example to security-governance\n\nTwo adversarially-verified deep-research passes (25/25 claims confirmed each,\n0 killed) close the two material gaps flagged in the topic review:\n\n- Supply-chain / SAST / SCA for AI-generated code: OSV-Scanner, Semgrep, Snyk,\n  Socket, CodeQL (what each scans, CI integration, license).\n- Incident response: OWASP AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet (primary-source\n  containment guidance), GitHub break-glass credential revocation, Claude Agent\n  SDK rewindFiles, STRATUS/TNR pre-execution rejection, kill-switch inadequacy\n  (Stanford Law + Palisade), and the PocketOS/Railway incident case study.\n\nWire all 11 pages into index.md (Tools/Patterns/Gaps) and reference-architecture.md\n(layer 7 + seam 3), and add a worked end-to-end example to the reference\narchitecture: one CI-PR scenario wiring all seven layers with illustrative\nconfig (Claude Code settings.json, default-deny egress, Rego PDP, CI SAST gate)\nand an honest callout of the three layers that remain seams even in a concrete build.\n\nManifest additions are purely additive; pages hand-catalogued (not auto-fetched).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd4f45011beca59c1b7b6bf9a7dd70d2f94471fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/git/trees/cd4f45011beca59c1b7b6bf9a7dd70d2f94471fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alcherkas/claude/git/commits/425de4