d75cffff"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/misshanya/PRODHugs/commit/742d4ff1e4fc3f19062e936d632fdc7a97644ede","sha":"742d4ff1e4fc3f19062e936d632fdc7a97644ede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/commits/742d4ff1e4fc3f19062e936d632fdc7a97644ede"}],"sha":"a98962c67fcafff522efaf17a1cd0d61bc524923","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/commits/a98962c67fcafff522efaf17a1cd0d61bc524923"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124452155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadim-Khristenko","id":124452155,"login":"Vadim-Khristenko","node_id":"U_kgDOB2r9Ow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/commits/742d4ff1e4fc3f19062e936d632fdc7a97644ede/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T15:47:15Z","email":"vadim@vai-rice.space","name":"Vadim Khristenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T15:47:15Z","email":"vadim@vai-rice.space","name":"Vadim Khristenko"},"message":"ci: fix smoke cascade, render help block as markdown, bump upload-artifact\n\nGFM doesn''t parse markdown inside inline HTML tags, so the help\nfooter''s backtick-wrapped commands rendered as literal text. Swap\nthe <sub> wrapper for a blockquote (\\>\\) — same visual demotion,\nmarkdown still renders. The signature line stays in <sub> since it\nhas no markdown to process.\n\nactions/upload-artifact bumped v4 -> v7 in both pr-checks.yml usages.\n\nSmoke tests were eating themselves on the per-IP auth rate limit:\nthe suite fires register-weak / register-user-A / register-dup /\nregister-user-B back-to-back from 127.0.0.1, and the limiter is\nburst=2 per hour on /auth/register — every subsequent register\nreturned 429, which then cascaded into 8 downstream failures (user\nB never existed, so note CRUD, profile, and @username search all\nbroke). Add an \"AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED\" env knob that the backend\nchecks at boot; the smoke step and smoke-backend.sh both export it\nso the middleware is skipped just for this run. Production is\nunaffected — the env var is absent in normal deployments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: AVRORA AI (27B) <avrora@vai-prog.ru>","tree":{"sha":"b5d90a1c6b2cce9bcafe9ab2f0f6fb1f0c250d69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/git/trees/b5d90a1c6b2cce9bcafe9ab2f0f6fb1f0c250d69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/git/commits/742d4ff1e4fc3f19062e936d632fdc7a97644ede","verification":{"payload":"tree b5d90a1c6b2cce9bcafe9ab2f0f6fb1f0c250d69\nparent c9baa6111302f50ed4d423bc2f098766d39ac8a3\nauthor Vadim Khristenko <vadim@vai-rice.space> 1779032835 +0300\ncommitter Vadim Khristenko <vadim@vai-rice.space> 1779032835 +0300\n\nci: fix smoke cascade, render help block as markdown, bump upload-artifact\n\nGFM doesn''t parse markdown inside inline HTML tags, so the help\nfooter''s backtick-wrapped commands rendered as literal text. Swap\nthe <sub> wrapper for a blockquote (\\>\\) — same visual demotion,\nmarkdown still renders. The signature line stays in <sub> since it\nhas no markdown to process.\n\nactions/upload-artifact bumped v4 -> v7 in both pr-checks.yml usages.\n\nSmoke tests were eating themselves on the per-IP auth rate limit:\nthe suite fires register-weak / register-user-A / register-dup /\nregister-user-B back-to-back from 127.0.0.1, and the limiter is\nburst=2 per hour on /auth/register — every subsequent register\nreturned 429, which then cascaded into 8 downstream failures (user\nB never existed, so note CRUD, profile, and @username search all\nbroke). Add an \"AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED\" env knob that the backend\nchecks at boot; the smoke step and smoke-backend.sh both export it\nso the middleware is skipped just for this run. Production is\nunaffected — the env var is absent in normal deployments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: AVRORA AI (27B) <avrora@vai-prog.ru>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRN+vYIq3SQEYMdx70r1Gio6+T07wUCagnjAxsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwyLDEACgkQK9RoqOvk9O/UEgEAjFeRYHpp8F4Be1NjMHxX\nW8aNxtn7BYfHs8PcVXikUMMBALZFDJddiVuVp/k4iYkqTp58PceZgYkJWTOveN2w\nQrIG\n=4/66\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-17T15:47:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124452155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadim-Khristenko","id":124452155,"login":"Vadim-Khristenko","node_id":"U_kgDOB2r9Ow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/misshanya/PRODHugs/commit/742d4ff1e4fc3f19062e936d632fdc7a97644ede","node_id":"C_kwDOSPTt1NoAKDc0MmQ0ZmYxZTRmYzNmMTkwNjJlOTM2ZDYzMmZkYzdhOTc2NDRlZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/misshanya/PRODHugs/commit/c9baa6111302f50ed4d423bc2f098766d39ac8a3","sha":"c9baa6111302f50ed4d423bc2f098766d39ac8a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/commits/c9baa6111302f50ed4d423bc2f098766d39ac8a3"}],"sha":"742d4ff1e4fc3f19062e936d632fdc7a97644ede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/commits/742d4ff1e4fc3f19062e936d632fdc7a97644ede"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124452155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadim-Khristenko","id":124452155,"login":"Vadim-Khristenko","node_id":"U_kgDOB2r9Ow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/commits/c9baa6111302f50ed4d423bc2f098766d39ac8a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T15:21:59Z","email":"vadim@vai-rice.space","name":"Vadim Khristenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T15:21:59Z","email":"vadim@vai-rice.space","name":"Vadim Khristenko"},"message":"ci: fix summarize.sh exit crash, deeper failure analysis, broader smoke\n\nsummarize.sh had two compounding bugs that combined to make any failed\nbackend run also break the report rendering:\n  1. \\grep -c ... || echo 0\\ doubled the count to \"0\\n0\" because grep\n     prints 0 to stdout AND exits 1 when there are no matches; the\n     integer compare below then exploded with \"integer expression\n     expected\". A new count_matches helper uses \\|| true\\ so grep''s\n     own count stands.\n  2. Every case branch in metric_for ended with \\[ N -gt 0 ] && echo …\\\n     — when the count was zero the && short-circuited, the branch\n     returned 1, and the function with it. Under the workflow''s\n     \\\bash -e {0}\\ (and the script''s own set -euo pipefail) this\n     killed the entire report step. All branches now use \\if … fi\\\n     and metric_for returns 0 explicitly.\n\nNew extract_findings prints a \"Что бросилось в глаза\" bullet block\nabove the captured-output details: top-N issues for lint, individual\ntest names (plus panic lines if any), the bullet of smoke FAIL\nlines, parsed eslint issues (file path + line:col + rule), and\ntypecheck errors. Metric column gained build/vet/typecheck counters\nand a \"N fail(s), M panic(s)\" composite for test.\n\nsmoke-backend.sh nearly doubled in scope: 18 checks vs 9. Added a\nSUMMARY footer so the result is unambiguous even when output is\ntruncated. New positive tests: @username search prefix, full note\nCRUD (PUT/GET/list/DELETE/404-after-delete), idempotent second\ndaily-reward claim, pair cooldown lookup. New negative tests: weak-\npassword register (expect 400/422), no-token /users/me (expect 401),\nduplicate username (expect 409/400). A new http_call helper trims\nthe duplication of curl-with-status-code-and-body-jar that the\nscript accumulated.\n\npr-bot.yml: hardcoded BOT_OWNERS list (currently vadim-khristenko)\nbypasses every permission check — the maintainer dev-mode escape\nhatch. /ci stays open to everyone. /label is now allowed for: bot\nowner, PR author, write+ collaborator, OR anyone whose commits are\nalready on the default branch (checked cheaply via listCommits with\nauthor filter and per_page=1). The \"not allowed\" reply was rewritten\nin Aurora''s voice with a longer, kinder hint about asking a\nmaintainer for access.\n\nCo-Authored-By: AVRORA AI (27B) <avrora@vai-prog.ru>","tree":{"sha":"541b919448789e1b63e66a33bd15d8654ee32d12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/git/trees/541b919448789e1b63e66a33bd15d8654ee32d12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/git/commits/c9baa6111302f50ed4d423bc2f098766d39ac8a3","verification":{"payload":"tree 541b919448789e1b63e66a33bd15d8654ee32d12\nparent 0c144c607eba28ba403928c99f7859d89525f9ea\nauthor Vadim Khristenko <vadim@vai-rice.space> 1779031319 +0300\ncommitter Vadim Khristenko <vadim@vai-rice.space> 1779031319 +0300\n\nci: fix summarize.sh exit crash, deeper failure analysis, broader smoke\n\nsummarize.sh had two compounding bugs that combined to make any failed\nbackend run also break the report rendering:\n  1. \\grep -c ... || echo 0\\ doubled the count to \"0\\n0\" because grep\n     prints 0 to stdout AND exits 1 when there are no matches; the\n     integer compare below then exploded with \"integer expression\n     expected\". A new count_matches helper uses \\|| true\\ so grep''s\n     own count stands.\n  2. Every case branch in metric_for ended with \\[ N -gt 0 ] && echo …\\\n     — when the count was zero the && short-circuited, the branch\n     returned 1, and the function with it. Under the workflow''s\n     \\\bash -e {0}\\ (and the script''s own set -euo pipefail) this\n     killed the entire report step. All branches now use \\if … fi\\\n     and metric_for returns 0 explicitly.\n\nNew extract_findings prints a \"Что бросилось в глаза\" bullet block\nabove the captured-output details: top-N issues for lint, individual\ntest names (plus panic lines if any), the bullet of smoke FAIL\nlines, parsed eslint issues (file path + line:col + rule), and\ntypecheck errors. Metric column gained build/vet/typecheck counters\nand a \"N fail(s), M panic(s)\" composite for test.\n\nsmoke-backend.sh nearly doubled in scope: 18 checks vs 9. Added a\nSUMMARY footer so the result is unambiguous even when output is\ntruncated. New positive tests: @username search prefix, full note\nCRUD (PUT/GET/list/DELETE/404-after-delete), idempotent second\ndaily-reward claim, pair cooldown lookup. New negative tests: weak-\npassword register (expect 400/422), no-token /users/me (expect 401),\nduplicate username (expect 409/400). A new http_call helper trims\nthe duplication of curl-with-status-code-and-body-jar that the\nscript accumulated.\n\npr-bot.yml: hardcoded BOT_OWNERS list (currently vadim-khristenko)\nbypasses every permission check — the maintainer dev-mode escape\nhatch. /ci stays open to everyone. /label is now allowed for: bot\nowner, PR author, write+ collaborator, OR anyone whose commits are\nalready on the default branch (checked cheaply via listCommits with\nauthor filter and per_page=1). The \"not allowed\" reply was rewritten\nin Aurora''s voice with a longer, kinder hint about asking a\nmaintainer for access.\n\nCo-Authored-By: AVRORA AI (27B) <avrora@vai-prog.ru>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRN+vYIq3SQEYMdx70r1Gio6+T07wUCagndFxsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwyLDEACgkQK9RoqOvk9O89nwEAp6lC3z01R7YcwrKGAEjq\nhNMuTjx7+YwP44u5DRcVzLIA/2DkQ3FuZtv6b95j0v8WF9pagCrLpv3QgDJELfpN\nBmkD\n=sK+H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-17T15:24:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124452155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/followers","following_