ived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/commits/0c144c607eba28ba403928c99f7859d89525f9ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T14:48:56Z","email":"vadim@vai-rice.space","name":"Vadim Khristenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T14:48:56Z","email":"vadim@vai-rice.space","name":"Vadim Khristenko"},"message":"ci(backend): add curl smoke-test job\n\nThe backend job now spins up postgres:18-alpine as a service container\nand runs a sequence of curl calls against a freshly built binary:\nservice start, /ping\", register, login, /users/me\", /api/v2/users/search\",\n/api/v2/users/@:name/profile\", /api/v2/daily-reward/status\", /balance\",\nand POST /daily-reward\". Each step reports OK or FAIL with a reason;\non any FAIL the script dumps the backend log tail so the PR comment\nhas something concrete to point at.\n\nThe smoke check is meant as a tripwire — it catches \"the service won''t\neven start\" or \"register/login regressed\" classes of bugs that pure\nbuild + lint never see. Real Go tests, when we have them, will go in\ngo test ./... and stack on top.\n\nCo-Authored-By: AVRORA AI (27B) <avrora@vai-prog.ru>","tree":{"sha":"0180167197c5d711a1ff999391c0d97393828bda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/git/trees/0180167197c5d711a1ff999391c0d97393828bda"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/git/commits/0c144c607eba28ba403928c99f7859d89525f9ea","verification":{"payload":"tree 0180167197c5d711a1ff999391c0d97393828bda\nparent a27258374273b70cce0c1aa3d0ccdd96b1e32c49\nauthor Vadim Khristenko <vadim@vai-rice.space> 1779029336 +0300\ncommitter Vadim Khristenko <vadim@vai-rice.space> 1779029336 +0300\n\nci(backend): add curl smoke-test job\n\nThe backend job now spins up postgres:18-alpine as a service container\nand runs a sequence of curl calls against a freshly built binary:\nservice start, /ping\", register, login, /users/me\", /api/v2/users/search\",\n/api/v2/users/@:name/profile\", /api/v2/daily-reward/status\", /balance\",\nand POST /daily-reward\". Each step reports OK or FAIL with a reason;\non any FAIL the script dumps the backend log tail so the PR comment\nhas something concrete to point at.\n\nThe smoke check is meant as a tripwire — it catches \"the service won''t\neven start\" or \"register/login regressed\" classes of bugs that pure\nbuild + lint never see. Real Go tests, when we have them, will go in\ngo test ./... and stack on top.\n\nCo-Authored-By: AVRORA AI (27B) <avrora@vai-prog.ru>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRN+vYIq3SQEYMdx70r1Gio6+T07wUCagnVWRsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwyLDEACgkQK9RoqOvk9O/zqAEAjGXEGcyIikUHhZdW3LV2\nliWUaqwOGjuxmRD6sViZES4BAOmoiqtl6JqSvtXGX/CuFIw6z0zierg1c2vCjLfC\n6FYG\n=84yq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-17T14:49:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124452155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadim-Khristenko","id":124452155,"login":"Vadim-Khristenko","node_id":"U_kgDOB2r9Ow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/misshanya/PRODHugs/commit/0c144c607eba28ba403928c99f7859d89525f9ea","node_id":"C_kwDOSPTt1NoAKDBjMTQ0YzYwN2ViYTI4YmE0MDM5MjhjOTlmNzg1OWQ4OTUyNWY5ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/misshanya/PRODHugs/commit/a27258374273b70cce0c1aa3d0ccdd96b1e32c49","sha":"a27258374273b70cce0c1aa3d0ccdd96b1e32c49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/commits/a27258374273b70cce0c1aa3d0ccdd96b1e32c49"}],"sha":"0c144c607eba28ba403928c99f7859d89525f9ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/commits/0c144c607eba28ba403928c99f7859d89525f9ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124452155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadim-Khristenko","id":124452155,"login":"Vadim-Khristenko","node_id":"U_kgDOB2r9Ow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/commits/a27258374273b70cce0c1aa3d0ccdd96b1e32c49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T14:37:35Z","email":"vadim@vai-rice.space","name":"Vadim Khristenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T14:37:35Z","email":"vadim@vai-rice.space","name":"Vadim Khristenko"},"message":"ci: fix sticky comment, add /ci rerun-from-comment, smarter reports\n\npost-comment.js: take owner / repo / issueNumber / body / marker as\nexplicit args. The previous version did \"{...context, payload: ...}\"\nto fake a different PR, but \\@actions/github\\ exposes \"context.repo\"\nas a getter on the class prototype, and spread doesn''t copy getters —\nso context.repo.owner blew up on the workflow_run path. Fail loud on\nmissing args while we''re here.\n\npr-comment.yml: bump actions/download-artifact to v8, force Node 24,\nand tolerate one of the two artifacts being absent (frontend-only or\nbackend-only PRs).\n\npr-checks.yml: add workflow_dispatch with pr_number / head_sha /\ntargets / skip_docker inputs. Setup job resolves whether we''re on\na PR (paths-filter) or a manual rerun (inputs.targets), and checks\nout head_sha explicitly. Concurrency group is scoped per-PR so a\nmanual rerun doesn''t kill a parallel pull_request run.\n\npr-bot.yml (new): listens to \"issue_comment.created\", parses \"/ci\" or\n\"@github-pr-bot\" commands, authorizes via getCollaboratorPermissionLevel\n(write+ only), reacts 👀/🚀/👎/😕, dispatches pr-checks with the parsed\nscope + skip-docker flag. workflow_dispatch fires on default_branch so\nthe workflow itself is always trusted; only the source we test\n(head_sha) comes from the PR.\n\nsummarize.sh: quick-fix block (copy-pasteable commands for the\nfailures actually present), metric column in the results table\n(lint issue count, test failure count, eslint problems), trigger\nlabel (pull_request vs manual rerun), separate commit/run/job links,\nand a slash-command tip in the footer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: AVRORA AI (27B) <avrora@vai-prog.ru>","tree":{"sha":"e7a83c6dc85b43854bdca70909b68e20c52883a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/git/trees/e7a83c6dc85b43854bdca70909b68e20c52883a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/misshanya/PRODHugs/git/commits/a27258374273b70cce0c1aa3d0ccdd96b1e32c49","verification":{"payload":"tree e7a83c6dc85b43854bdca70909b68e20c52883a3\nparent b978052fd01ab88f4a86ea68d4b23307d75cffff\nauthor Vadim Khristenko <vadim@vai-rice.space> 1779028655 +0300\ncommitter Vadim Khristenko <vadim@vai-rice.space> 1779028655 +0300\n\nci: fix sticky comment, add /ci rerun-from-comment, smarter reports\n\npost-comment.js: take owner / repo / issueNumber / body / marker as\nexplicit args. The previous version did \"{...context, payload: ...}\"\nto fake a different PR, but \\@actions/github\\ exposes \"context.repo\"\nas a getter on the class prototype, and spread doesn''t copy getters —\nso context.repo.owner blew up on the workflow_run path. Fail loud on\nmissing args while we''re here.\n\npr-comment.yml: bump actions/download-artifact to v8, force Node 24,\nand tolerate one of the two artifacts being absent (frontend-only or\nbackend-only PRs).\n\npr-checks.yml: add workflow_dispatch with pr_number / head_sha /\ntargets / skip_docker inputs. Setup job resolves whether we''re on\na PR (paths-filter) or a manual rerun (inputs.targets), and checks\nout head_sha explicitly. Concurrency group is scoped per-PR so a\nmanual rerun doesn''t kill a parallel pull_request run.\n\npr-bot.yml (new): listens to \"issue_comment.created\", parses \"/ci\" or\n\"@github-pr-bot\" commands, authorizes via getCollaboratorPermissionLevel\n(write+ only), reacts 👀/🚀/👎/😕, dispatches pr-checks with the parsed\nscope + skip-docker flag. workflow_dispatch fires on default_branch so\nthe workflow itself is always trusted; only the source we test\n(head_sha) comes from the PR.\n\nsummarize.sh: quick-fix block (copy-pasteable commands for the\nfailures actually present), metric column in the results table\n(lint issue count, test failure count, eslint problems), trigger\nlabel (pull_request vs manual rerun), separate commit/run/job links,\nand a slash-command tip in the footer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: AVRORA AI (27B) <avrora@vai-prog.ru>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRN+vYIq3SQEYMdx70r1Gio6+T07wUCagnSrxsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwyLDEACgkQK9RoqOvk9O8fnwEAh+OYMmWuJvO/yE0m2O66\nYJm+fBLEtzkU017JOg8UjowA/3/JqYO0oxja14hBtoE3FGEwTYXr9HWMdqfJ0shg\ncVIL\n=SiRZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-17T14:49:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124452155?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadim-Khristenko","id":124452155,"login":"Vadim-Khristenko","node_id":"U_kgDOB2r9Ow","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadim-Khristenko","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/misshanya/PRODHugs/commit/a27258374273b70cce0c1aa3d0ccdd96b1e32c49","node_id":"C_kwDOSPTt1NoAKGEyNzI1ODM3NDI3M2I3MGNjZTBjMWFhM2QwY2NkZDk2YjFlMzJjNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/misshanya/PRODHugs/commit/b978052fd01ab88f4a86ea68d4b23307d75cffff","sha":"b978052fd01ab88f4a86